{
  "title": "Dua Jawshan al Kabir",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Jawshan means “chain armour”, worn to protect the body against weapons.\nIn one of the early wars the Almighty Allah sent the text of this dua to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) from that day he discarded the armour and used to recite this dua in every battlefield.\nKafa’mee has mentioned this dua in his books “Balaadul Ameen” and “Misbah”, on the authority of Imam Ali bin Husain Al Zaynul A’abideen (a.s.) who learned it from his father, Imam Husain (a.s.), the grandson of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nIt is a many-sided all-purpose dua. For and on behalf of him who recites Jawshan Kabeer in the beginning of the Holy month of Ramazan, an army of seventy thousand Angels sing praises of the Almighty Allah, earning (for him) due recompense and reward.\nIf recited 3 times during the Holy month of Ramazan (particularly on “Shab-e-Qadr” nights) fire of Hell will refuse to burn the reciter and as a result the gates of paradise will be thrown open for him, because as soon as it is recited Almighty Allah takes him under his protection and keeps him safe from the onslaught of sinful temptations.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) advised Imam Ali (a.s.), Bibi Faatemah (s.a.), Imam Hasan (a.s.), and Imam Husain (a.s.) to learn it by heart and recite again and again because it contains “Ism-e-A’azam” (the Great name of Allah), and make sure to tell people to write this dua on the cloth of shroud before a dead faithful person is buried as it is the best defence against all types of punishments and penalties; above all the fire of Hell will not dare to touch him.\nAt the time of war it is the most reliable defence for the faithfuls.\nRecite it before going on a journey to come back safe and successful.\nIf written text is kept in the house it is a safe insurance against fire, theft, loot and arson.\nIf written text is kept on person as Taweez it drives away misfortunes, keeps clear of accidents and brings prosperity.\nThis dua, in addition to the Holy month of Ramazan, should be recited on Fridays.\nRecite this dua once a month or at any time during a year if you are a “very busy person”, and even if that is not possible for reasons beyond your control, recite it at least once in your lifetime.\nIn all there are 100 sections in this Dua; and, in each section, 10 names or attributes of Almighty Allah are mentioned, except section 55, in which 11 attributes are recited.\nAt the end of each section recite the following:\nسُبْحَانَكَ يَا لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ \nSUBHAANAKA YAA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTAL \nGlory be to You, O “there is no god save You”, \nالْغَوْثَ الْغَوْثَ خَلِصَّنَا مِنَ النَّارِ يَا رَبْ.\nGAUSAL GAUS KHALLISNAA MENAN NAARE YAA RAB.\nHelp! Help! Keep away the Fire from us, O Lord,\n(1) For Success in Difficult Works:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْٓ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا اَللهُ یَارَحْمٰنُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA ALLAAHO, YAA RAHMAAN, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Allah, O The Beneficent, \nیَا رَحِیْمُ یَا كَرِیْمُ یَامُقِیْمُ یَاعَظِیْمُ\nYAA RAHEEMO, YAA KAREEMO, YAA MOQEEMO, YAA A’ZEEMO, \nO The Merciful, O the Generous, O The Self-Subsisting, O The Great,\nیَا قَدِیْمُ یَا عَلِیْمُ یَا حَلِیْمُ یَا حَكِیْمُ.\nYAA QADEEMO, YAA A’LEEMO, YAA HALEEMO, YAA HAKEEMO.\nO The Eternal, O The All-Wise, O The Indulgent, O The All-Knowing.\n(2) To Seek Help\nیَاسَیِّدَ السَّادَاتِ یَا مُجِیْبَ الدَّعْوَاتِ \nYAA SAYYEDAS SAADAATE, YAA MOJEEBAD DAAWAATE, \nO The chief of chiefs, O The Answerer of Prayers, \nیَارَافِعَ الدَّرَجَاتِ یَا وَلِیَّ الْحَسَنَاتِ \nYAA RAFE-A’D DARAJAATE, YAA WALIYYAL HASANAATE, \nO The Raiser of Ranks, O The Bestower of benefits, \nیَا غَافِرَ الْخَطِیْئَآتِ یَا مُعْطِیَ الْمَسْئَلَاتِ \nYAA GHAAFERAL KHATI-A’ATE, YAA MO’TEYAL MAS-ALAATE \nO The Forgiver of sins, O The Granter of requests, \nیَا قَابِلَ التَّوْبَاتِ یَا سَامِعَ الْاَصْوَاتِ \nYAA QABEELAT TAWBAATE, YAA SAAME-A’L ASWAATE, \nO The Acceptor of repentance, O The Hearer of voices, \nیَا عَالِمَ الْخَفِیَّاتِ یَا دَافِعَ الْبَلِیَّاتِ.\nYAA A’ALEMAL KHAFIYYAATE, YAA DAAFE-A’L BALIYYAATE.\nO The Knower of mysteries, O The Disperser of misfortunes.\n(3) To Attain Honour And Dignity\nیَاخَیْرَ الْغَافِرِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْفَاتِحِیْنَ \nYAA KHAYRAL GHAAFEREENA, YAA KHAYRAL FAATEHEENA, \nO The Best of forgivers, O The Best of conquerors, \nیَا خَیْرَ النَّاصِرِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْحَاكِمِیْنَ \nYAA KHAYRAN NAASEREENA, YAA KHAYRAL HAAKEMEENA, \nO The Best of helpers, O The Best of arbitrators, \nیَا خَیْرَ الرَّازِقِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْوَارِثِیْنَ \nYAA KHAYRAR RAAZEQEENA, YAA KHAYRAL WAARESEENA, \nO The Best of nourishers, O The Best of survivors, \nیَا خَیْرَ الْحَامِدِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الذَّاكِرِیْنَ \nYAA KHAYRAL HAAMEDEENA, YAA KHAYRAZ ZAAKEREENA, \nO The Best of admirers, O The Best of rememberers, \nیَا خَیْرَ الْمُنْزِلِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْمُحْسِنِیْنَ.\nYAA KHAYRAL MUNZELEENA, YAA KHAYRAL MOHSENEENA.\nO The Best of providers, O The Best of benefactors.\n(4) To Acquire Nobility In Both The Worlds\nیَا مَنْ لَهُ الْعِزَّۃُ وَ الْجَمَالُ یَا مَنْ لَهُ الْقُدْرَۃُ وَ الْكَمَالُ \nYAA MAN LAHUL I’ZZATO WAL JAMAALO, YAA MAN LAHUL QUDRATO WAL KAMAALO, \nO He for Whom is glory and beauty, O He for Whom is authority and perfection, \nیَا مَنْ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَ الْجَلَالُ یَا مَنْ هُوَ الْكَبِیْرُ الْمُتَعَالِ \nYAA MAN LAHUL MULKO WAL JALAALO, YAA MAN HOWAL KABEERUL MOTA-A’ALO, \nO He for Whom is kingdom and majesty, O He Who is Powerful and supreme, \nیَا مُنْشِءَ السَّحَابِ الثِّقَالِ یَا مَنْ هُوَ شَدِیْدُ الْمِحَالِ \nYAA MUNSHE’AS SAHAABIS SEQAALE, YAA MAN HOWA SHADEEDUL MEHAALE, \nO He Who raises the heavy clouds, O He Who is firm in strategy, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ سَرِیْعُ الْحِسَابِ یَا مَنْ هُوَ شَدِیْدُ الْعِقَابِ \nYAA MAN HOWA SAREE-U’L HESAABE, YAA MAN HOWA SHADEEDUL E’QAABE, \nO He Who is severe in punishment, O He Who is alert in reckoning, \nیَا مَنْ عِنْدَهٗ حُسْنُ الثَّوَابِ یَا مَنْ عِنْدَهٗ اُمُّ الْكِتَابِ.\nYAA MAN I’NDAHU HUSNAS SAWAABE, YAA MAN I’NDAHU UMMUL KETAABE.\nO He Who gives excellent reward, O He Who has “Ummul Kitab’ (the Mother Book).\n(5) To Achieve Renown And Success\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْٓ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا حَنَّانُ یَا مَنَّانُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA HANNAANO, YAA MANNAANO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Kind, O Benevolent, \nیَا دَیَّانُ یَا بُرْهَانُ یَا سُلْطَانُ یَا رِضْوَانُ \nYAA DAYYAANO, YAA BURHAANO, YAA SULTAANO, YAA RIZWAANO, \nO Requiter, O Clear Sign, O Sovereign, O Gratifier, \nیَا غُفْرَانُ یَا سُبْحَانُ یَا مُسْتَعَانُ یَا ذَا الْمَنِّ وَ الْبَیَانِ.\nYAA GHUFRAANO, YAA SUBHAANO, YAA MUSTA-A’ANO, YAA ZALMANNE WAL BAYAANE.\nO Forgiver, O Praiseworthy, O He Who is called upon for help, O Master of destiny and demonstration. \n(6) To Obtain Blessings And Ranks\nیَا مَنْ تَوَاضَعَ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ لِعَظَمَتِهٖ \nYAA MAN TAWAAZA-A’ KULLO SHAY-I’N LE AZAMATEHI, \nO He! Everything behaves with humility before Whose greatness, \nیَا مَنِ اسْتَسْلَمَ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ لِقُدْرَتِهٖ \nYAA MANIS TASLAMA KULLO SHAY-IN LE-QUDRATEHI, \nO He! Everything surrenders to Whose power, \nیَا مَنْ ذَلَّ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ لِعِزَّتِهٖ \nYAA MAN ZALLA KULLO SHAY-IN LE-I’ZZATEHI, \nO He! Everything submits to Whose authority, \nیَا مَنْ خَضَعَ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ لِهَیْبَتِهٖ \nYAA MAN KHAZA-A’ KULLO SHAY-IN LEHAYBATEHI, \nO He! Everything yields to Whose majesty, \nیَا مَنِ انْقَادَ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ مِنْ خَشْیَتِهٖ \nYAA MANIN QADA KULLO SHAY-IN MIN KHASYATEHI, \nO He! Everything abides by Whose fear, \nیَا مَنْ تَشَقَّتِ الْجِبَالُ مِنْ مَخَافَتِهٖ \nYAA MAN TASHAQQATIL JEBAALO MIN MAKHAAFATEHI, \nO He! Mountains rend asunder by Whose awe, \nیَا مَنْ قَامَتِ السَّمٰوَاتُ بِاَمْرِهٖ \nYAA MAN QAAMATIS SAMAWAATO BE-AMREHI, \nO He! The heavens have stood still under Whose command, \nیَا مَنِ اسْتَقَرَّتِ الْاَرْضُوْنَ بِاِذْنِهٖ \nYAA MANIS TAQARRATIL ARZOONA BE-IZNEHI, \nO He! The earths have settled down by Whose leave, \nیَا مَنْ یُّسَبِّحُ الرَّعْدُ بِحَمْدِهٖ \nYAA MANY YOSABBEHUR RA’DO BE-HAMDEHI, \nO He! The thunder sings Whose praise, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَعْتَدِیْ عَلٰٓی اَهْلَ مَمْلَكَتِهٖ.\nYAA MAN LAA YA’TADI A’LAA AHLE MAMLAKATEHI.\nO He! Who does not terrorize His subjects.\n(7) To Disperse Calamities\nیَا غَافِرَ الْخَطَایَا یَا كَاشِفَ الْبَلَایَا \nYAA GHAAFERAL KHATAAYAA, YAA KAASHEFAL BALAAYAA \nO Pardoner of errors, O Disperser of afflictions, \nیَا مُنْتَهَی الرَّجَایَا یَا مُجْزِلَ الْعَطَایَا \nYAA MUNTAHAR RAJAAYAA, YAA MUJZELAL A’TAAYAA, \nO Ultimate means of relief, O Awarder of rewards, \nیَا وَاهِبَ الْهَدَایَا یَا رَازِقَ الْبَرَایَا \nYAA WAAHEBAL HADAAYAA, YAA RAAZEQAL BARAAYAA, \nO Liberal Donator of calm and peace, O Giver of daily bread to creatures, \nیَا قَاضِیَ الْمَنَایَا یَا سَامِعَ الشَّكَایَا \nYAA QAAZEYAL MONAAYAA, YAA SAAMEASH SHAKAAYAA, \nO Executor of just decrees, O Hearer of complaints, \nیَا بَاعِثَ الْبَرَایَا یَا مُطْلِقَ الْاُسَارٰی.\nYAA BAA-E’SAL BARAAYAA, YAA MUTLAQAL OSAARAA.\nO Author of creation, O Liberator of prisoners.\n(8) To Ask Pardon\nیَا ذَا الْحَمْدِ وَالثَّنَآءِ یَا ذَا الْفَخْرِ وَالْبَهَآءِ \nYAA ZAL HAMDE WAS SANAA-E, YAA ZAL FAKHRE WAL BAHAA-E, \nO Focus of praise and adoration, O Possessor of pride and eminence, \nیَا ذَا الْمَجْدِ وَالسَّنَآءِ یَا ذَا الْعَهْدِ وَالْوَفَآءِ \nYAA ZAL MAJDE WAS SANAA-E YAA ZAL AHDE WAL WAFAA-E \nO Master of dignity and sublimity, O Covenanter and fulfiller of promises, \nیَا ذَا الْعَفْوِ وَ الرَّضَاءِ یَا ذَا الْمَنِّ وَالْعَطَآءِ \nYAA ZAL AFVE WAR RAZAA-E, YAA ZALMANNE WAL ATAA-E, \nO Excuser and Agreer, O Benefactor, and Bestower, \nیَا ذَا الْفَضْلِ وَالْقَضَآءِ یَا ذَا الْعِزِّ وَ الْبَقَآءِ \nYAA ZAL FAZLE WAL QAZAA-E, YAA ZAL I’ZZE WAL BAQAA-E, \nO Kind and (Just) Judge, O Glorious and Eternal, \nیَا ذَا الْجُوْدِ وَالسَّخَآءِ یَا ذَا الْآلَآءِ وَالنَّعْمَآءِ.\nYAA ZAL JOODE WAS SAKHAA-E YAA ZAL AALAA-E WAN NAAMAA-E.\nO Munificent and Bounteous, O High and Benign.\n(9) To Clear Away Fear And Disease\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْٓ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا مَانِعُ یَا دَافِعُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA,YAA MAANE-O’, YAA DAAFE-O’, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Preventer, O Disperser, \nیَارَافِعُ یَا صَانِعُ یَا نَافِعُ یَا سَامِعُ \nYAA RAAFE-O YAA SAANE-O YAA NAAFE-O’, YAA SAAME-O’, \nO Raiser, O Maker, O Benefactor, O Listener, \nیَا جَامِعُ یَا شَافِعُ یَاوَاسِعُ یَامُوْسِعُ.\nYAA JAAME-O YAA SHAAFE-O YAA WAASE-O’, YAA MOOSE-O’.\nO Gatherer, O Rescuer, O Enricher, O Increaser.\n‍‍‍(10) To Get Approval Of Conduct\nیَا صَانِعَ كُلِّ مَصْنُوْعٍ یَا خَالِقَ كُلِّ مَخْلُوْقٍ \nYAA SAANE-A KULLE MASNOO-I’N, YAA KHAALEQA KULLE MAKHLOOQIN, \nO maker of all that has been made, O Creator of all that has been created, \nیَا رَازِقَ كُلِّ مَرْزُوْقٍ یَا مَالِكَ كُلِّ مَمْلُوْكٍ \nYAA RAAZEQA KULLE MARZOOQIN, YAA MAALEKA KULLE MAMLOOKIN. \nO Provider of daily bread to all who are in need of food, O Master of all servants (whole creation), \nیَا كَاشِفَ كُلِّ مَكْرُوْبٍ یَا فَارِجَ كُلِّ مَهْمُوْمٍ \nYA KAASHEFA KULLE MAKROOBIN, YAA FAAREJA KULLE MAHMOOMIN, \nO Expeller of all hardships, O Reliever of all grief and sorrow, \nیَا رَاحِمَ كُلِّ مَرْحُوْمٍ یَا نَاصِرَ كُلِّ مَخْذُوْلٍ \nYAA RAAHEMA KULLE MARHOOMIN, YAA NAASERA KULLE MAKHZOOLIN, \nO Merciful to all those who seek mercy, O Helper of all those who have been forsaken, \nیَا سَاتِرَ كُلِّ مَعْیُوْبٍ یَا مَلْجَاَ كُلِّ مَطْرُوْدٍ.\nYAA SAATERA KULLE MA’YOOBIN, YAA MALJA-A KULLE MATROODIN.\nO Concealer of all defects, O Refuge of all those who have been thrown out.\n(11) To Avoid Evil And Gain Prosperity\nیَا عُدَّتِیْ عِنْدَ شِدَّتِیْ یَا رَجَآئِیْ عِنْدَ مُصِیْبَتِیْ \nYAA UDDATI I’NDA SHIDDATI, YAA RAJAA-E’E I’NDA MOSEEBATI, \nO My Support in my hardship, O my Hope in my misfortune, \nیَا مُوْنِسِیْ عِنْدَ وَحْشَتِیْ یَا صَاحِبِیْ عِنْدَ غُرْبَتِیْ \nYAA MOONESI I’NDA WAH-SHATEE, YAA SAAHEBEE I’NDA GHOORBATI, \nO my Sympathizer in my loneliness, O my Companion in my journey, \nیَا وَلِیِّیْ عِنْدَ نِعْمَتِیْ یَا غِیَاثِیْ عِنْدَ كُرْبَتِیْ \nYAA WALIYYEE I’NDA NE’MATEE, YAA GHEYAASEE I’NDA KOORBATEE, \nO my Ally in my happiness, O my Supporter in my distress, \nیَا دَلِیْلِیْ عِنْدَ حَیْرَتِیْ یَا غَنَآئِیْ عِنْدَ افْتِقَارِیْ \nYAA DALEELEE I’NDA HAYRATEE, YAA GHENAA-E’E I’NDAF TEQAARI \nO my Guide in my confusion, O my Advantage in my bliss, \nیَا مَلْجَائِیْ عِنْدَ اضْطِرَارِیْ یَا مُعِیْنِیْ عِنْدَ مَفْزَعِیْ.\nYAA MALJA-E’E I’NDAZ TERAAREE, YAA MO-E’ENEE I’NDA MAFZA-E’E.\nO my Sanctuary in my misery, O my Succourer in my despair.\n‍(12) To Dismiss Affliction and Secure Good Fortune\nیَا عَلاَّمَ الْغُیُوْبِ یَا غَفَّارَ الذُّنُوْبِ \nYAA A’LLAAMAL GHOYOOBE, YAA GHAFFAARAZ ZONOOBE \nO Perceiver of the invisible, O Coverer of fault, \nیَا سَتَّارَ الْعُیُوْبِ یَا كَاشِفَ الْكُرُوْبِ \nYAA SATTAARAL O’YOOBE, YAA KAASHEFAL KOROOBE, \nO Concealer of shortcomings, O Reliever of pains, \nیَا مُقَلِّبَ الْقُلُوْبِ یَا مُنَوِّرَ الْقُلُوْبِ \nYAA MOQALLEBAL QOLOOBE, YAA TABEEBAL QOLOOBE \nO Converter of hearts, O Healer of hearts, \nیَا طَبِیْبَ الْقُلُوْبِ یَا اَنِیْسَ الْقُلُوْبِ \nYAA MONAWWERAL QOLOOBE YAA ANEESAL QOLOOBE, \nO Enlightner of hearts, O Consoler of hearts, \nیَا مُفَرِّجَ الْهُمُوْمِ یَا مُنَفِّسَ الْغُمُوْمِ.\nYAA MOFARREJAL HOMOOME, YAA MONAFFESAL GHOMOOME.\nO Dispeller of worries, O Disperser of grieves.\n(13) To Cure Eye Disease\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا جَلِیْلُ یَا جَمِیْلُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA JALEELO, YAA JAMEELO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your Name, O Magnificent, O Elegant, \nیَا وَكَیْلُ یَا كَفِیْلُ یَا دَلِیْلُ یَا قَبِیْلُ \nYAA WAKEELO, YAA KAFEELO, YAA DALEELO, YAA QABEELO, \nO Protector, O Satisfier, O Demonstrator, O Guarantor, \nیَا مُدِیْلُ یَا مُنِیْلُ یَا مُقِیْلُ یَا مُحِیْلُ.\nYAA MODEELO, YAA MONEELO, YAA MOQEELO YAA MOHEELO.\nO Enricher, O Favourer, O Acquitter, O Vivifier.\n(14) To Increase Wealth\nیَا دَلِیْلَ الْمُتَحَیِّرِیْنَ یَا غِیَاثَ الْمُسْتَغِیْثِیْنَ \nYAA DALEELAL MOTAHAYYAREENA, YAA GHEYAASAL MUSTAGHEESEENA, \nO Guide of the bewildered, O Helper of the help-seekers, \nیَا صَرِیْخَ الْمُسْتَصْرِخِیْنَ یَا جَارَ الْمُسْتَجِیْرِیْنَ \nYAA SAREEKHAL MUSTASREKHEENA, YAA JAARAL MUSTAJEEREENA, \nO Answerer to the out criers, O Protector of the protection-seekers, \nیَآ اَمَانَ الْخَآئِفِیْنَ یَا عَوْنَ الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ \nYAA AMAANAL KHAA-E-FEENA, YAA AWNAL MO’MENEENA, \nO Asylum for the afraid, O Escort of the faithful, \nیَا رَاحِمَ الْمَسَاكِیْنَ یَا مَلْجَاَ الْعَاصِیْنَ \nYAA RAAHEMAL MASAAKEENA, YAA MAL-JA-A’L A’ASEENA, \nO Provider of the poor, O Hope of the disobedient, \nیَا غَافِرَ الْمُذْنِبِیْنَ یَا مُجِیْبَ دَعْوَۃِ الْمُضْطَرِّیْنَ.\nYAA GHAAFERAL MUZNEBEENA, YAA MOJEEBA DA’WATIL MUZTARREENA.\nO Pardoner of the sinners, O Comforter of the restless.\n(15) To Ask For More Benefits\nیَا ذَا الْجُوْدِ وَالْاِحْسَانِ یَا ذَا الْفَضْلِ وَالْاِمْتِنَانِ \nYAA ZAL JOODE WAL EHSAANE, YAA ZAL FAZLE WAL IMTENAANE, \nO Lord of abundance and benefits, O Lord of superabundance and favours, \nیَا ذَا الْاَمْنِ وَالْاَمَانِ یَا ذَا الْقُدْسِ وَالسُّبْحَانِ \nYAA ZAL AMNE WAL AMAANE, YAA ZAL QUDSE WAS SUBHAANE, \nO Lord of peace and security, O Lord of purity and glory, \nیَا ذَا الْحِكْمَۃِ وَالْبَیَانِ یَا ذَا الرَّحْمَۃِ وَالرِّضْوَانِ \nYAA ZAL HIKMATE WAL BAYAANE, YAA ZAR-RAHMATE WAR RIZWAANE, \nO Lord of wisdom and evidence, O Lord of mercy and approval, \nیَا ذَا الْحُجَّۃِ وَالْبُرْهَانِ یَا ذَا الْعَظَمَۃِ وَالسُّلْطَانِ \nYAA ZAL HUJJATE WAL BURHAANE, YAA ZAL A’ZMATE WAS SULTAANE, \nO Lord of argument and proof, O Lord of grandeur and sovereignty, \nیَا ذَا الرَّافَۃِ وَالْمُسْتَعَانِ یَا ذَا الْعَفْوِ وَالْغُفْرَانِ.\nYAA ZAR RAAFATE WAL MUSTA-A’ANE, YAA ZAL A’FVE WAL GHUFRAANE.\nO Lord of sublimity and support, O Lord of amnesty and forgiveness.\n(16) To Solve Problems\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ رَبُّ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ یَا مَنْ هُوَ اِلٰهُ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ \nYAA MAN HOWA RABBO KULLE SHAY-IN, YAA MAN HOWA ELAAHO KULLE SHAY-IN, \nO He Who is the provider of means of livelihood to everything, O He Who is God of everything, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ یَا مَنْ هُوَ صَانِعُ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ \nYAA MAN HOWA KHAALEQO KULLE SHAY-IN, YAA MAN HOWA SAALEHO KULLE SHAY-IN, \nO He Who is the Creator of everything, O He Who is the Fashioner of everything, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ یَا مَنْ هُوَ بَعْدَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ \nYAA MAN HOWA QABLA KULLE SHAY-IN, YAA MAN HOWA BA’DA KULLE SHAY-IN, \nO He Who is prior to everything, O He Who is beyond everything, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فَوْقَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ یَا مَنْ هُوَ عَالِمٌ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ \nYAA MAN HOWA FAWQA KULLE SHAY-IN, YAA MAN HOWA A’ALEMUN BEKULLE SHAY-IN, \nO He Who is over and above everything, O He Who is Knower of everything, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ قَادِرٌ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ یَا مَنْ هُوَ یَبْقٰی وَ یَفْنٰی كُلُّ شَیْءٍ.\nYAA MAN HOWA QAADERUN A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN, YAA MAN HOWA YABQAA WA YAFNAA KULLE SHAY-IN.\nO He Who is Dominant over everything, O He Who is Ever-Living while everything dies.\n(17) To Accomplish Difficult Undertakings\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا مُؤْمِنُ یَا مُهَیْمِنُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA MO’MENO YAA MOHAYMENO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name O Genuine, O Guardian, \nیَا مُكَوِّنُ یَا مُلَقِّنُ یَا مُبَیِّنُ یَا مُهَوِّنُ \nYAA MOKAWWENO YAA MOLAQQENO, YAA MOBAYYENO YAA MOHAWWENO \nO Self-Existing, O Addresser (to the dead), O Revealer, O Gentle, \nیَا مُمَكِّنُ یَا مُزَیِّنُ یَا مُعْلِنُ یَا مُقَسِّمُ.\nYAA MOMAKKENO, YAA MOZAYYENO, YAA MO’LENO, YAA MOQASSEMO.\nO Accomplisher, O Beautifier, O Proclaimer, O Distributor.\n(18) To Increase Livelihood\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ مُلْكِهٖ مُقِیْمٌ یَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ سُلْطَانِهٖ قَدِیْمٌ \nYAA MAN HOWA FEE MULKEHI MOQEEMUN, YAA MAN HOWA FEE SULTAANEHI QADEEMUN, \nO He Who is Ever-Abiding in His (boundless) kingdom, O He Who is forever powerful in His absolute power, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ جَلاَلِهٖ عَظِیْمٌ یَا مَنْ هُوَ عَلٰی عِبَادِهٖ رَحِیْمٌ \nYAA MAN HOWA FEE JALAALEHI A’ZEEMUN, YAA MAN HOWA A’LAA E’BAADEHI RAHEEMUN, \nO He Who is Great in His majesty, O He Who is Merciful to His servants, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ عَلِیْمٌ یَا مَنْ هُوَ بِمَنْ عَصَاهُ حَلِیْمٌ \nYAA MAN HOWA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEMUN, YAA MAN HOWA BE-MAN A’SAAHO HALEEMUN, \nO He Who is fully aware of all things, O He Who is Forbearing towards the disobedient, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ بِمَنْ رَجَاهُ كَرِیْمٌ یَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ صُنْعِهٖ حَكِیْمٌ \nYAA MAN HOWA BE-MAN RAJAAHO KAREEMUN, YAA MAN HOWA FEE SUN-EHI HAKEEMUN, \nO He Who is Gener-ous to the requester, O He Who is Wise in His act of creating, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ حِكْمَتِهٖ لَطِیْفٌ یَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ لُطْفِهٖ قَدِیْمٌ.\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE HIKMATEHI LATEEFUN, YAA MAN HOWA FEE LUTFEHI QADEEMUN.\nO He Who is Subtle in His wisdom, O He Who is ever more Benign in his benevolence.\n(19) To Attain Distinction\nیَا مَنْ لَا یُرْجٰی اِلَّا فَضْلُهٗ یَا مَنْ لَا یُسْئَلُ اِلَّا عَفْوُهٗ \nYAA MAN LAA YURJAA ILLA FAZLAHU, YAA MAN LAA YUS-A’LO ILLAA A’FWOHU, \nO He from whom nothing but favor is expected, O He from Whom nothing but pardon is obtained, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یُنْظَرُ اِلَّا بِرُّهٗ یَا مَنْ لَا یُخَافُ اِلَّا عَدْلُهٗ \nYAA MAN LAA YUNZARO ILLAA BIRROHU, YAA MAN LA YOKHAAFO ILLAA A’DLOHU, \nO He from Who nothing but good comes out, O He Who is not feared but for His justice, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یَدُوْمُ اِلَّا مُلْكُهٗ یَا مَنْ لَا سُلْطَانَ اِلَّا سُلْطَانُهٗ \nYAA MAN LA YADOOMO ILLAA MULKAHU, YAA MAN LAA SULTAANA ILLA SULTAANOHU, \nO He Whose Kingdom alone (and nothing) is eternal, O He Whose Sovereignty alone (and nothing) is prevailing, \nیَا مَنْ وَسِعَتْ كُلَّ شَیْءٍ رَحْمَتُهٗ یَا مَنْ سَبَقَتْ رَحْمَتُهٗ غَضَبَهٗ \nYAA MAN WASE-A’T KULLA SHAY-IN RAHMATOHU, YAA MAN SABAQAT RAHMATOHU GHAZABAHU, \nO He Whose Mercy encompasses everything, O He Whose compassion gets the better of His wrath, \nیَا مَنْ اَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ عِلْمُهٗ یَا مَنْ لَیْسَ اَحَدٌ مِثْلَهٗ.\nYAA MAN AHAATA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN I’LMOHU, YAA MAN LAYSA AHADUNN MISLOHU.\nO He Whose wisdom comprehends everything, O He Who has no equal.\n(20) To Disperse Worries \nیَا فَارِجَ الْهَمِّ یَا كَاشِفَ الْغَمِّ \nYAA FAAREJAL HAMME, YAA KAASHEFAL GHAMME, \nO Disperser of worry, O Mitigator of sorrow, \nیَا غَافِرَ الذَّنْبِ یَا قَابِلَ التَّوْبِ \nYAA GHAAFERAZ ZAMBE, YAA QAABELAT TAWBE, \nO Forgiver of Sins, O Acceptor of repentance, \nیَا خَالِقَ الْخَلْقِ یَا صَادِقَ الْوَعْدِ \nYAA KHAALEQAL KHALQE, YAA SAADEQAL WA’DE \nO Creator of creation, O Sincere Fulfiller of promises, \nیَا مُوْفِیَ الْعَهْدِ یَا عَالِمَ السِّرِّ \nYAA MOOFEYAL A’HDE YAA A’ALEMAS SIRRE, \nO Accomplisher of covenants, O Knower of secrets, \nیَا فَالِقَ الْحَبِّ یَا رَازِقَ الْاَنَامِ.\nYAA FAALEQAL HABBE, YAA RAAZEQAL ANAAME.\nO Splitter of seed, O Sustainer of mankind.\n(21) To Plead For Forgiveness Of Sins\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا عَلِیُّ یَا وَفِیُّ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA A’LIYYO, YAA WAFIYYO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O High, O Perfect, \nیَا غِنِیُّ یَا مَلِیُّ یَا حَفِیُّ یَا رِضِیُّ \nYAA GHANIYYO, YAA MALIYYO, YAA KHAFIYYO, YAA RAZIYYO, \nO Independent, O Rich, O Hidden, O Assenter, \nیَا زَكِیُّ یَا بَدِیُّ یَا قَوِیُّ یَا وَلِیُّ.\nYAA ZAKIYYO, YAA BADIYYO, YAA QAWIYYO, YAA WALIYYO.\nO Intelligent, O First, O Mighty, O Guardian.\n(22) To Increase Livelihood\nیَا مَنْ اَظْهَرَ الْجَمِیْلَ \nYAA MAN AZHARAL JAMEEL \nO He Who exposes beauty, \nوَ يَا مَنْ سَتَرَ الْقَبِیْحَ \nWA YAA MAN SATARAL QABEEHA \nO He Who conceals ugliness, \nوَ یَا مَنْ لَّمْ یُؤَاخِذُ بِالْجَرِیْرَۃِ \nWA YAA MAN LAM YO-AAKHIZ BIL JARIRATE \nO He Who does not call to account for transgressions, \nوَ یَا مَنْ لَّمْ یَهْتِكِ السِّتْرَ \nWA YAA MAN LAM YAHTEKIS SITRA, \nO He Who does not withdraw protection, \nیَا عَظِیْمَ الْعَفْوِ یَا حَسَنَ التَّجَاوُزِ \nYAA A’ZEEMAL A’FVE YAA HASANAT TAJAAWOZE, \nO The Great Forgiver, O Dispensator of fair treatment, \nیَا وَاسِعَ الْمَغْفِرَۃِ یَا بَاسِطَ الْیَدَیْنِ بِالرَّحْمَۃِ \nYAA WAASE-A’L MAGHFERATE, YAA BAASETAL YADAYNE BIRRAHMATE, \nO Boundless forgiver, O Spreader of unlimited mercy, \nیَا صَاحِبَ كُلِّ نَجْوٰی یَا مُنْتَهٰی كُلِّ شَكْوٰی.\nYAA SAAHEBA KULLE NAJWAA, YAA MUNTAHAA KULLE SHAKWAA.\nO Sharer of mutual secrets, O Last Resort of all complaints.\n(23) To Get More Beneficence\nیَا ذَا النِّعْمَۃِ السَّابِغَۃِ\nYAA ZAN NE-A’MATIS SAABEGHATE, \nO Master of abundant bounties, \nیَا ذَالرَّحْمَۃِ الْوَاسِعَۃِ\nYAA ZARRAHMATIL WAASE-A’TE, \nO Master of plenteous mercy, \nیَا ذَا الْمِنَّۃِ السَّابِقَۃِ\nYAA ZALMINNATIS SAABEQATE, \nO Master of incomparable kindness, \nیَا ذَا الْحِكْمَۃِ الْبَالِغَۃِ\nYAA ZAL HIKMATIL BAALEGHATE,\nO Master of penetrating wisdom, \nیَا ذَا الْقُدْرَۃِ الْكَامِلَۃِ\nYAA ZAL QUDRATIL KAAMELATE, \nO Master of absolute power,\nیَا ذَا الْحُجَّۃِ الْقَاطِعَۃِ\nYAA ZAL HUJJATIL QAATE-A’TE,\nO Master of conclusive argument,\nیَا ذَا الْكَرَامَۃِ الظَّاهِرَۃِ\nYAA ZAL KARAAMATIZ ZAAHERATE,\nO Master of evident generosity, \nیَا ذَا الْعِزَّۃِ الدَّآئِمَۃِ\nYAA ZAL I’ZZATID DAA-EMATE,\nO Master of everlasting dignity, \nیَا ذَا الْقُوَّۃِ الْمَتِیْنَۃِ\nYAA ZAL QUWWATIL MATEENATE,\nO Master of strong might, \nیَا ذَا الْعَظَمَۃِ الْمَنِیْعَۃِ.\nYAA ZAL A’ZAMATIL MANEE-A’TE.\nO Master of impregnable greatness.\n(24) To Receive Allah’s Bliss\nیَا بَدِیْعَ السَّمٰوٰتِ یَا جَاعِلَ الظُّلُمَاتِ\nYAA BADEEA’S SAMAAWAATE, YAA JAA-E’LAZ ZOLOMAATE, \nO Creator of heavens, O Activator of Darkness, \nیَا رَاحِمَ الْعَبَرَاتِ یَا مُقِیْلَ الْعَثَرَاتِ\nYAA RAAHEMAL ABARAATE, YAA MOQEELAL ASARAATE,\nO Pitier of tears, O Ignorer of errors, \nیَا سَاتِرَ الْعَوْرَاتِ یَا مُحْیِیَ الْاَمْوَاتِ\nYAA SAATERAL AWRAATE, YAA MOH-YEYAL AMWAATE,\nO Concealer of ignominy, O Revivifier of the dead, \nیَا مُنْزِلَ الْاٰیاَتِ یَا مُضَعِّفَ الْحَسَنَاتِ\nYAA MUNZELAL-AAYAATE, YAA MOZA’-E’FAL HASANAATE, \nO Revealer of signs, O Multiplier of virtues, \nیَا مَاحِیَ السَّیِّئَاتِ یَا شَدِیْدَ النَّقِمَاتِ.\nYAA MAAHEYAS SAYYE-AATE, YAA SHADEEDAN NAQEMAATE.\nO Obliterator of vices, O Severe Reckoner.\n(25) To Dispel Ill Luck And Seek Fortune\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا مُصَوِّرُ یَا مُقَدِّرُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA MOSAWWERO, YAA MOQADDERO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Fashioner, O Pre-Ordainer, \nیَا مُدَبِّرُ یَامُطَهِّرُ یَا مُنَوِّرُ یَا مُیَسِّرُ\nYAA MODABBERO, YAA MOTAH-HERO, YAA MONAWWERO YAA MOYASSERO, \nO Statesman, O Purifier, O Illuminator, O Sufficer, \nیَا مُبَشِّرُ یَا مُنْذِرُ یَا مُقَدِّمُ یَا مُؤَخِّرُ.\nYAA MOBASH-SHERO, YAA MONAZ-ZERO, YAA MOQAD-DEMO, YAA MO-A’KH-KHERO.\nO Communicator of glad tidings, O Warner, O Foremost, O Postponer.\n(26) To Get Rid Of Fever\nیَا رَبَّ الْبَیْتِ الْحَرَامِ یَا رَبَّ الشَّهْرِ الْحَرَامِ\nYAA RABBAL BAYTIL HARAAME, YAA RABBASH SHAHRIL HARAAME, \nO Lord of the Holy House, O Lord of the Holy month, \n\nیَا رَبَّ الْبَلَدِ الْحَرَامِ یَا رَبَّ الرُّكْنِ وَالْمَقَامِ\nYAA RABBAL BALAADIL HARAAME,YAA RABBAR-RUKNE WAL MAQAAME,\nO Lord of the Holy city, O Lord of Rukn (Trust) and Maqaam (Dignity), \nیَا رَبَّ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ يَا رَبَّ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ\nYAA RABBAL MASH-A’RIL HARAAME, YAA RABBAL MASJEDIL HARAAME,\nO Lord of Mashril Haraam, (Place where Hajis pray and offer sacrifice), O Lord of the Holy Mosque, \nیَا رَبَّ الْحِلِّ وَالْحَرَامِ یَا رَبَّ النُّوْرِ وَالظَّلَامِ\nYAA RABBAL HILLE WAL HARAAME, YAA RABBAN NOORE WAZ ZALAAME, \nO Lord (Ordainer) of Hill (Lawful) and Haraam (Unlawful), O Lord of light and darkness, \nیَا رَبَّ التَّحِیَّۃِ وَ السَّلَامِ یَا رَبَّ الْقُدْرَۃِ فِی الْاَنَامِ.\nYAA RABBAT TAHIYYATE WAS SALAAME, YAA RABBAL QOODRATE FIL ANAAME.\nO Lord of life (Keeping alive) and peace, O Lord of might over created beings.\n(27) To Dismiss Fear Of Rulers (Recite 20 times)\nیَآ اَحْكَمَ الْحَاكِمِیْنَ یَا اَعْدَلَ الْعَادِلِیْنَ\nYAA AHKAMAL HAAKEMEENA YAA A-A’DALAL A’ADELEENA, \nO The Wisest of all rulers, O The Most equitable of all judges, \nیَآ اَصْدَقَ الصَّادِقِیْنَ یَا اَطْهَرَ الطَّاهِرِیْنَ\nYAA ASDAQAS SAADEQEENA, YAA ATHARAT TAAHEREENA, \nO The Truest of the true, O The Purest of the pure, \nیَآ اَحْسَنَ الْخَالِقِیْنَ یَا اَسْرَعَ الْحَاسِبِیْنَ\nYAA AHSANAL KHAALEQEENA, YAA ASRA-A’L HAASEBEENA, \nO The Best of all creators, O The Quickest of all reckoner, \nیَا اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِیْنَ یَا اَبْصَرَ النَّاظِرِیْنَ\nYAA ASMA-A’S SAAME-E’ENA, YAA ABSARAN NAAZEREENA, \nO The Best of all hearers, O The Best of all observers, \nیَآ اَشْفَعَ الشَّافِعِیْنَ یَا اَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِیْنَ.\nYAA ASHFA-A’SH SHAAFE-E’ENA, YAA AKRAMAL AKRAMEENA.\nO The Best of all intercessors, O The Most Noble of all nobles.\n‍(28) To Cure Migraine\nیَاعِمَادَ مَنْ لَا عِمَادَ لَهٗ یَا سَنَدَ مَنْ لَا سَنَدَ لَهٗ\nYAA E’MAADA MAN LAA E’MAADA LAHU, YAA SANADA MAN LAA SANADA LAHU, \nO Support of him who has no support, O Surety of him who has nothing to lean upon,\nیَا ذُخْرَ مَنْ لَا ذُخْرَلَهٗ یَا حِرزَ مَنْ لَا حِرْزَلَهٗ\nYAA ZUKHRA MAN LAA ZUKHRA LAHU, YAA HIRZA MAN LA HIRZA LAHU, \nO Repository of him who has no provision, O Protection of him who has no protection, \nیَا غِیَاثَ مَنْ لَا غِیَاثَ لَهٗ یَا فَخْرَ مَنْ لَا فَخْرَ لَهٗ\nYAA GHEYAASA MAN LAA GHEYAASA LAHU, YAA FAKHRA MAN LAA FAKHRA LAHU, \nO Succourer of him who has been forsaken, O Pride of him who has nothing to be proud of, \nیَا عِزَّ مَنْ لَا عِزَّ لَهٗ یَا مُعِیْنَ مَنْ لَا مُعِیْنَ لَهٗ\nYAA I’ZZA MAN LA I’ZZA LAHU, YAA MO-E’ENA MAN LAA MO-E’ENA LAHU, \nO Glory of him who has no distinction, O Help of him who is helpless, \nیَا اَنِیْسَ مَنْ لَا اَنِیْسَ لَهٗ یَا اَمَانَ مَنْ لَا اَمَانَ لَهٗ.\nYAA ANEESA MAN LAA ANEESA LAHU, YAA AMAANA MAN LAA AMANA LAHU.\nO Companion of him who has no comrade, O Refuge of him who has no shelter. \n(29) To Build Up Defense\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا عَاصِمُ یَا قَآئِمُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA A’ASEMO, QAA-EMO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Defender, O Ever-Lasting, \nیَا دَآئِمُ یَا رَاحِمُ یَا سَالِمُ یَاحَاكِمُ\nYAA DAA-E’MO, YAA RAAHEMO, YAA SAALEMO YAA HAKEMO, \nO Ever-Living, O Merciful, O Dependable, O Ruler, \nیَا عَالِمُ یَا قَاسِمُ یَا قَابِضُ یَا بَاسِطُ.\nYAA A’ALEMO, YAA QAASEMO, YAA QAABEZO, YAA BAASETO.\nO Knower, O Distributor, O Seizer, O Expansive.\n(30) To Win War\nیَا عَاصِمَ مَنِ اسْتَعْصَمَهٗ\nYAA A’ASEMA MANIS TA’SAMAHU,\nO Defender of him who seeks His aid, \nیَا رَاحِمَ مَنِ اسْتَرْحَمَهٗ\nYAA RAAHEMA MANIS TARHAMAHU,\nO Pitier of him who seeks His mercy,\nیَا غَافِرَ مَنِ اسْتَغْفَرَهٗ\nYAA GHAAFERA MANIS TAGHFERAHU, \nO Pardoner of him who seeks His pardon, \nیَا نَاصِرَ مَنِ اسْتَنْصَرَهٗ\nYAA NAASERA MANIS TANSARAHU, \nO Rescuer of him who seeks His aid, \nیَا حَافِظَ مَنِ اسْتَحْفَظَهٗ\nYAA HAAFEZA MANIS TAHFAZAHU \nO Protector of him who seeks His protection, \nیَا مُكْرِمَ مَنِ اسْتَكْرَمَهٗ\nYAA MUKREMA MANIS TAKRAMAHU,\nO Favourer of him who seeks His favour, \nیَا مُرْشِدَ مَنِ اسْتَرْشَدَهٗ\nYAA MURSHEDA MANIS TARSHADAHU,\nO Leader of him who seeks His guidance, \nیَا صَرِیْخَ مَنِ اسْتَصْرَخَهٗ\nYAA SAREEKHA MANIS TASRAKHAHU,\nO Succourer of him who seeks His succour, \nیَا مُعِیْنَ مَنِ اسْتَعَانَهٗ\nYAA MO-E’ENA MANIS TA-A’ANAHU,\nO Helper of him who seeks His help, \nیَا مُغِیْثَ مَنِ اسْتَغَاثَهٗ.\nYAA MOGHEESA MANIS TAGHASAHU.\nO Supporter of him who seeks His support.\n(31) To Cure Eye Disease\nیَا عَزِیْزًا لَّا یُضَامُ یَا لَطِیْفًا لَّا یُرَامُ\nYAA A’ZEEZAN LAA YOZAAMO, YAA LATEEFAL LAA YORAAMO, \nO Great Who is never humbled, O Subtle Who is unperceivable, \nیَا قَیُّوْمًا لَّا یَنَامُ یَا دَآئِمًا لَّا یَفُوْتُ\nYAA QAYYOOMAL LAA YANAAMO, YAA DAA-EMAL LAA YAFOOTO, \nO Durable Who slumbers not, O Ever-Lasting Who is indestructible, \nیَا حَیًّا لَّا یَمُوْتُ یَا مَلِكًا لَّا یَزُوْلُ\nYAA HAYYAN LAA YAMOOTO, YAA MALEKAL LAA YAZOOLO, \nO Ever-Living Who is not mortal, O Master Who never loses control, \nیَا بَاقِیًا لَّا یَفْنٰی یَا عَالِمًا لَّا یَجْهَلُ\nYAA BAAQEYAL LAA YAFNAA, YAA A’ALEMAL LAA YAJHALO, \nO Eternal Who is never non-existent, O Knower Who is never ignorant, \nیَا صَمَدًا لَّا یُطْعَمُ یَا قَوِیًّا لَّا یَضْعُفُ.\nYAA SAMADAL LAA YUT-A’MO, YAA QAWIYYAL LAA YUZ-A’FO.\nO Endurer Who needs no sustenance, O Mighty Who is never undermined.\n(32) To Subdue Enemies\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا اَحَدُ یَا وَاحِدُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA AHADO, YAA WAAHEDO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Single, O One, \nیَا شَاهِدُ یَا مَاجِدُ یَا حَامِدُ یَا رَاشِدُ \nYAA SHAAHEDO , YAA MAAJEDO, YAA HAAMEDO YAA RAASHEDO, \nO Witness, O Praised, O Glorious, O Guide, \nیَا بَاعِثُ یَا وَارِثُ یَا ضَآرُّ یَا نَافِعُ.\nYAA BAA-ESO, YAA WAARESO, YAA ZAARRO, YAA NAAFE-O’.\nO Author, O Possessor, O Punisher, O Benefactor.\n(33) To Have Courage To Face Rulers\nيَا اَعْظَمَ مِنْ كُلِّ عَظِيْمٍ \nYAA A-A’ZAMA MIN KULLE A’ZEEMIN, \nO The Supreme among (all) the chiefs, \nيَا اَكْرَمَ مِنْ كُلِّ كَرِيْمٍ\nYAA AKRAMA MIN KULLE KAREEMIN, \nO The Most Generous among (all) the generous, \nيَا اَرْحَمَ مِنْ كُلِّ رَحِيْمٍ\nYAA ARHAMA MIN KULLE RAHEEMIN, \nO The Most Merciful among (all) the Merciful, \nيَا اَعْلَمَ مِنْ كُلِّ عَلِيْمٍ\nYAA A-A’LAMA MIN KULLE A’LEEMIN \nO the Most Learned among (all) the learned, \nيَا اَحْكَمَ مِنْ كُلِّ حَكِيْمٍ\nYAA AHKAMA MIN KULLE HAKEEMIN, \nO The Wisest among (all) the wise, \nيَا اَقْدَمَ مِنْ كُلِّ قَدِيْمٍ\nYAA AQDAMA MIN KULLE QADEEMIN, \nO The Foremost among (all) the formers, \nيَا اَكْبَرَ مِنْ كُلِّ كَبِيْرٍ\nYAA AKBARA MIN KULLE KABEERIN, \nO The Greatest among (all) the greats, \nيَا اَلْطَفَ مِنْ كُلِّ لَطِيْفٍ\nYAA ALTAFA MIN KULLE LATEEFIN, \nO The Most Subtle among (all) the refined, \nيَا اَجَلَّ مِنْ كُلِّ جَلِيْلٍ\nYAA AJALLA MIN KULLE JALEELIN, \nO The Most Sublime among (all) the magnificent, \nيَا اَعَزَّ مِنْ كُلِّ عَزِيْزٍ.\nYAA A-A’ZZA MIN KULLE A’ZEEZIN.\nO The Mightiest among (all) the mighty.\n(34) To Seek Safeguard Against Jinn\nیَا كَرِیْمَ الصَّفْحِ یَا عَظِیْمَ الْمَنِّ\nYAA KAREEMAS SAFHE, YAA A’ZEEMAL MANNE, \nO Generous pardoner, O Great Benefactor, \nیَا كَثِیْرَ الْخَیْرِ یَا قَدِیْمَ الْفَضْلِ\nYAA KASEERAL KHAYRE, YAA QADEEMAL FAZLE, \nO Abounding Effecter of goodness, O Foremost Superabundant, \nیَا دَآئِمَ اللُّطْفِ یَا لَطِیْفَ الصُّنْعِ\nYAA DAA-E’MAL LUTFE, YAA LATIFAS SUN-E’, \nO Ever Kind, O Subtle Maker, \nیَا مُنَفِّسَ الْكَرْبِ یَا كَاشِفَ الضُّرِّ\nYAA MONAFFESAL KARBE, YAA KASHEFAZ ZURRE, \nO Reliever of pain, O Supplementer of damage, \nیَا مَالِكَ الْمُلْكِ یَا قَاضِیَ الْحَقِّ.\nYAA MAALEKAL MULKE, YAA KAAZEYAL HAQQE.\nO Lord of the realm, O The Just Judge.\n(35) To Cure Toothache\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ عَهْدِهٖ وَ فِیٌّ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE A’HDEHI WAFIYYUN, \nO He Who keeps His word sincerely, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ وَفَآئِهٖ قَوِیٌّ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE WAFAA-E’HI QAWIYYUN \nO He Who is strong in sincerity, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ قُوَّتِهٖ عَلِیٌّ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE QUWWATEHI A’LIYYUN, \nO He Who is High in strength, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ عُلُوِّهٖ قَرِیْبٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE OLUWWEHI QAREEBUN, \nO He Who is Near in highness,\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ قُرْبِهٖ لَطِیْفٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE QURBEHI LATEEFUN, \nO He Who is Subtle in nearness, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ لُطْفِهٖ شَرِیْفٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE LUTFEHI SHAREEFUN, \nO He Who is Noble in Subtility, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ شَرَفِهٖ عَزِیْزٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE SHARAFEHI A’ZEEZUN \nO He Who is Mighty in nobility, \nيَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ عِزِّهٖ عَظِیْمٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE I’ZZEHI A’ZEEMUN, \nO He Who is Great in might, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ عَظَمَتِهٖ مَجِیْدٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE A’ZAMATEHI MAJEEDUN, \nO He Who is Glorious in greatness, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ مَجْدِهٖ حَمِیْدٌ.\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE MAJEEDEHI HAMEEDUN.\nO He Who is praiseworthy in glory.\n(36) To Seek Protection Against Jinn\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا كَافِیْ یَا شَافِیْ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA KAAFEE, YAA SHAAFEE,\nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Adequate, O Curer, \nیَا وَافِیْ یَا مُعَافِیْ یَا هَادِیْ یَا دَاعِیْ\nYAA WAAFEE YAA MO-A’AFEE, YAA HAADEE, YAA DAAE’E,\nO Fulfiller, O Acquitter, O Shower of the right path, O Summoner, \nيَا قَاضِیْ یَا رَاضِیْ یَا عَالِیْ یَا بَاقِیْ.\nYAA QAAZEE, YAA RAAZEE, YAA A’ALEE, YAA BAAQEE.\nO Judge, O Consentient, O High, O Survivor.\n(37) To Win Battle\nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ خَاضِعٌ لَهٗ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN KHAAZEO’ON LAHU, \nO He to Whom all things bow down, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ خَاشِعٌ لَهٗ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN KHAASHEO’ON LAHU, \nO He to Whom all things submit, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ كَآئِنٌ لَهٗ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN KAA-E’NUN LAHU, \nO He for Whom all things persevere, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ مَّوْجُوْدٌ بِهٖ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN MAWJOODUN LAHU, \nO He for Whom all things exist, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ مُنِیْبٌ اِلَیْهِ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN MONEEBUN ELAYHE, \nO He towards Whom all things turn to, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ خَآئِفٌ مِنْهُ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN KHAA-E’FUN MINHO, \nO He! All things are afraid of Whom, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ قَآئِمٌ بِهٖ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN QAA-E’MUN BEHI, \nO He because of Whom all things endure, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ صَآئِرٌ اِلَیْهِ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN SAA-E’RUN ELAYHE \nO He towards Whom all things draw near, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ یُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهٖ\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN YOSABBEHO BE-HAMDEHI, \nO He Whom all things glorify with praise, \nیَا مَنْ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ هَالِكٌ اِلَّا وَجْهَهٗ.\nYAA MAN KULLO SHAY-IN HAALEKUN ILLAA WAJHOHU.\nO He except Who all things die.\n(38) To Seek Allah’s Help \nیَا مَنْ لَا مَفَرَّ اِلَّا اِلَیْهِ \nYAA MAN LAA MAFARRA ILLAA ELAYHE, \nO He aside from Whom there is no asylum, \nیَا مَنْ لَا مَفْزَعَ اِلَّا اِلَیْهِ \nYAA MAN LAA MAFZA-A’ ILLAA ELAYHE, \nO He aside from Whom there is no refuge, \nیَا مَنْ لَا مَقْصَدَ اِلَّا اِلَیْهِ \nYAA MAN LAA MAQSADA ILLAA ELAYHE, \nO He aside from Whom there is no destination, \nیَا مَنْ لَا مَنْجٰی مِنْهُ اِلَّا اِلَیْهِ \nYAA MAN LA MANJA MINHO ILLAA ELAYHE, \nO he aside from Whom there is no place of escape, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یُرْغَبُ اِلَّا اِلَیْهِ \nYAA MAN LA YARGHABO ILLAA ELAYHE, \nO He aside from Whom there is no one to lean upon, \nیَا مَنْ لَا حَوْلَ وَ لَا قُوَّۃَ اِلَّا بِهٖ \nYAA MAN LA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BEHI, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, has power and might, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یُسْتَعَانُ اِلَّا بِهٖ \nYAA MAN LA YUSTA-A’ANO ILLAA BEHI, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, is called upon for help, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یَتَوَكَّلُ اِلَّا عَلَیْهِ \nYAA MAN LAA YATAWAKKALO ILLAA A’LAIHE, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, is relied upon, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یُرْجٰی اِلَّا هُوَ \nYAA MAN LAA YURJAA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, is hopefully looked forward to, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یُعْبَدُ اِلَّا هُوَ.\nYAA MAN LA YA’BODO ILLAA HOWA.\nO He Who alone, and no one else, is worshipped.\n(39) To Overwhelm The Enemy \nیَا خَیْرَ الْمَرْهُوْبِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْمَرْغُوْبِیْنَ\nYAA KHAYRAL MARHOOBEENA, YAA KHAYRAL MARGHOOBEENA, \nO The Best of those (who are) feared, O The Best of those (who are) held dear, \nیَا خَیْرَ الْمَطْلُوْبِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْمَسْئُوْلِیْنَ\nYAA KHAYRAL MATLOOBEENA YA KHAYRAL MAS-OOLEENA, \nO The Best of those (who are) sought after, O The Best of those (who are) besought, \nیَا خَیْرَ الْمَقْصُوْدِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْمَذْكُوْرِیْنَ\nYAA KHAYRAL MAQSOODEENA, YAA KHAYRAL MAZKOOREENA, \nO The Best of those (who are) longed for, O The Best of those (who are) remembered, \nیَا خَیْرَ الْمَشْكُوْرِیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْمَحْبُوْبِیْنَ\nYAA KHAYRAL MASHKOOREENA, YAA KHAYRAL MAHBOOBEENA, \nO The Best of those (who are) thankfully acknowledged, O The Best of those (who are) adored, \nیَا خَیْرَ الْمَدْعُوِّیْنَ یَا خَیْرَ الْمُسْتَأنِسِیْنَ.\nYAA KHAYRAL MAD-O’OWEENA, YAA KHAYRAL MOOSTAA-NESEENA.\nO The Best of those (who are) called upon, O The Best of those (who are) befriended.\n(40) To Seek Forgiveness \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا غَافِرُ یَا سَاتِرُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA GHAAFERO, YAA SAATERO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Absolver, O Coverer, \nیَا قَادِرُ یَا قَاهِرُ یَا فَاطِرُ یَا كَاسِرُ \nYAA QAADERO, YAA QAAHERO, YAA FAATERO, YAA KAASERO, \nO Absolute, O Victor, O Maker, O Wrecker, \nیَاجَابِرُ یَا ذَاكِرُ یَا نَاظِرُ یَا نَاصِرُ.\nYAA JAABERO, YAA ZAAKERO, YAA NAAZERO, YAA NAASERO.\nO Assembler, O Relater, O Onlooker, O Succourer.\n(41) To Disperse Hot Poisonous Winds\nیَا مَنْ خَلَقَ فَسَوّٰی یَا مَنْ قَدَّرَ فَهَدٰی\nYAA MAN KHALAQA FASAWWAA, YAA MAN QADDARA FAHADAA, \nO He Who created and arranged (the creation) systematically, O He Who made laws and (thus) showed the right path, \nیَا مَنْ یَّكْشِفُ الْبَلْوٰی یَا مَنْ یَسْمَعُ النَّجْوٰی\nYAA MANY YAKSHEFUL BALWAA, YAA MANY YASMA-U’N NAJWAA, \nO He Who disperses calamities, O He Who hears the whispering secrets, \nیَا مَنْ یُنْقِدُ الْغَرْقٰی یَا مَنْ یُنْجِیَ الْهَلْكٰی\nYAA MANY YUNQEZUL GHARQAA, YAA MANY YUNJIL HALKAA, \nO He Who comes to the rescue of those who have been overwhelmed, O He Who saves from the danger of annihilation, \nیَا مَنْ یَّشْفِی الْمَرْضٰی یَا مَنْ اَضْحَكَ وَ اَبْكٰی\nYAA MANY YASHFIL MARZA YAA MAN AZHAKA WA ABKAA, \nO He Who cures the sick, O He Who brings about happiness and grief, \nیَا مَنْ اَمَاتَ وَ اَحْیٰی یَا مَنْ خَلَقَ الزَّوجَیْنِ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰی.\nYAA MAN AMAATA WA AHYAA YAA MAN KHALAQAZ ZAWJAYNAZ ZAKARA WAL UNSAA.\nO He Who puts to death and brings to life, O He Who created pairs, male and female.\n(42) To Seek Safeguard Against Calamities\nیَا مَنْ فِی الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ سَبِیْلُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-BARRE WAL-BAHRE SABEELOHU \nO He Who has means and ways on the land and in the seas, \nیَا مَنْ فِیْ الْآفَاقِ اٰیٰتُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-AAFAAQE AAYAATOHU, \nO He Whose signs are visible all over the universe, \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْاٰیَاتِ بُرْهَانُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-AAYAATE BURHAANOHU, \nO He Whose signs are clear arguments, \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْمَمَاتِ قُدْرَتُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-MAMAATE QUDRATOHU \nO He Who controls through mortality, \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْقُبُوْرِ عِبْرَتُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-QOBOORE I’BRATOHU, \nO He Who makes graves draw attention to His warning, \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْقِیٰمَۃِ مُلْكُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-QAYAAMATE MOLKOHU, \nO He Who owns the Day of Resurrection, \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْحِسَابِ هَیْبَتُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-HESAABE HAYBATOHU, \nO He Who overawes through the Day of reckoning, \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْمِیْزَانِ قَضَآؤُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-MEEZAANE QAZAA-OHU, \nO He Who passes judgment after scaling (good and bad), \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْجَنَّۃِ ثَوَابُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-JANNATE SAWAABOHU, \nO He Who awards paradise as reward, \nیَا مَنْ فِی النَّارِ عِقَابُهٗ.\nYAA MAN FINNAARE E’QAABOHU.\nO He Who condemns to Hell as a punishment.\n(43) To Have The Patronage Of The Wealthy\nیَا مَنْ اِلَیْهِ یَهْرَبُ الْخَآئِفُوْنُ\nYAA MAN ELAYHE YAHREBUL KHAAEFOONA, \nO He towards Who run the frightened, \nیَا مَنْ اِلَیْهِ یَفْزَعُ الْمُذْنِبُوْنُ \nYAA MAN ELAYHE YAFZA-U’L MUZNEBOONA, \nO He towards Whom flee the sinners (for help), \nیَا مَنْ اِلَیْهِ یَقْصِدُ الْمُنِیْبُوْنَ \nYAA MAN ELAYHE YAQSADUL MONEEBOONA \nO He towards Whom move the repentant, \nیَا مَنْ اِلَیْهِ یَرْغَبُ الزَّاهِدُوْنُ\nYAA MAN ELAYHE YARGHABUZ ZAAHEDOONA, \nO He to Whom turn the pious, \nیَا مَنْ اِلَیْهِ یَلْجَاءُ الْمُتَحَیِّرُوْنَ\nYAA MAN ELAYHE YALJAUL MOTAHAYYEROONA, \nO He with Whom the bewildered take refuge, \nیَا مَنْ بِهٖ یَسْتَاْنِسُ الْمُرِیْدُوْنُ\nYAA MAN BEHI YASTAANESUL MOREEDOONA, \nO He with Whom the entirely devoted become familiar, \nیَا مَنْ بِهٖ یَفْتَخِرُ الْمُحِبُّوْنُ\nYAA MAN BEHI YAFTAKHERUL MOHIBBOONA, \nO He of Whom the lovers are proud, \nیَا مَنْ فِی عَفْوِهٖ یَطْمَعُ الْخَاطِئُوْنَ\nYAA MAN FEE A’FVEHI YATMA-U’L KHAATE-OONA, \nO He Whose forgiveness the transgressors long for, \nیَا مَنْ اِلَیْهِ یَسْكُنُ الْمُوْقِنُوْنَ\nYAA MAN ELAYHE YASKONUL MOOQENOONA, \nO He in Whom the believers find peace, \nیَا مَنْ عَلَیْهِ یَتَوَكَّلُ الْمُتَوَكِّلُوْنَ.\nYAA MAN ELAYHE YATAWAKKALUL MOTAWAKKELOONA.\nO He upon Whom the trusting rely.\n(44) To Cultivate Love And Friendship\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا حَبِیْبُ یَا طَبِیْبُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA HABEEBO, YAA TABEEBO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Friend, O Doctor, \nیَا قَرِیْبُ یَا رَقِیْبُ یَا حَسِیْبُ یَا مُهِیْبُ\nYAA QAREEBO, YAA RAQEEBO, YAA HASEEBO, YAA MOHEEBO \nO Near, O Preserver, O Reckoner, O Awe-Inspiring, \nیَا مُثِیْبُ یَا مُجِیْبُ یَا خَبِیْرُ یَا بَصِیْرُ.\nYAA MOSEEBO, YAA MOJEEBO, YAA KHABEERO, YAA BASEERO.\nO Requiter, O Hearer of prayers, O All-Knowing, O All-Seeing. \n(45) To Get Rid Of Fearful Dreams \nیَا اَقْرَبَ مِنْ كُلِّ قَرِیْبٍ\nYAA AQRABA MIN KULLE QAREEBIN, \nO The Nearest of all nears, \nیَا اَحَبَّ مَنْ كُلَّ حَبِیْبٍ\nYAA AHABBA MIN KULLE HABEEBIN, \nO The Dearest of all dears, \nیَا اَبْصَرَ مِنْ كُلِّ بَصِیْرٍ \nYAA ABSARA MIN KULLE BASEERIN \nO The Most Discerning of all discerners, \nیَا اَخْبَرَ مِنْ كُلِّ خَبِیْرٍ \nYAA AKHBARA MIN KULLE KHABEERIN, \nO The Most Aware of all well-informed, \nیَا اَشْرَفَ مِنْ كُلِّ شَرِیْفٍ \nYAA ASHRAFA MIN KULLE SHAREEFIN, \nO The Noblest of all nobles, \nیَا اَرْفَعَ مِنْ كُلِّ رَفِیْعِ \nYAA ARFA-A’ MIN KULLE RAFEE-I’N, \nO The Most Exalted of all exalted, \nیَا اَقْوٰی مِنْ كُلِّ قَوِیٍّ \nYAA AQWAA MIN KULLE QAWIYYIN, \nO The Mightiest of all powerfuls, \nیَا اَغْنٰی مِنْ كُلِّ غَنِیٍّ \nYAA AGHNA MIN KULLE GHANIYYIN, \nO The Most Independent of all independents, \nیَا اَجْوَدَ مِنْ كُلِّ جَوَادٍ\nYAA AJWADA MIN KULLE JAWAADIN, \nO The Most Generous of all bountifuls, \nیَا اَرْئَفَ مِنْ كُلِّ رَءُوْفٍ.\nYAA AR-A’FA MIN KULLE RA-O’OFIN.\nO The Most Compassionate of all pardoners.\n(46) To Cure Infantile Paralysis\nیَا غَالِبًا غَیْرَ مَغْلُوْبٍ\nYAA GHAALEBAN GHAYRA MAGHLOOBIN, \nO Conqueror (Who is) not conquered,\nیَا صَانِعًا غَیْرَ مَصْنُوْعٍ\nYAA SAANE-A’N GHAYRA MASNOO-I’N, \nO Maker (Who is) not made, \nیَا خَالِقًا غَیْرَ مَخْلُوْقٍ\nYAA KHAALEQAN GHAYRA MAKHLOOQIN, \nO Creator (Who is) not created, \nیَا مَالِكًا غَیْرَ مَمْلُوْكٍ\nYAA MAALEKAN GHAYRA MAMLOOKIN, \nO Owner (Who is) not owned, \nیَا قَاهِرًا غَیْرَ مَقْهُوْرٍ \nYAA QAHERAN GHAYRA MAQHOORIN, \nO Subduer (Who is) not subdued, \nیَا رَافِعًا غَیْرَ مَرْفَوْعٍ\nYAA RAAFE-A’N GHAYRA MARFOO-I’N \nO Raiser (Who is) not raised, \nیَا حَافِظًا غَیْرَ مَحْفُوْظٍ\nYAA HAAFEZAN GHAYRA MAHFOOZIN, \nO Guardian (Who is) not guarded, \nیَا نَاصِرًا غَیْرَ مَنْصُوْرٍ\nYAA NAASERAN GHAYRA MANSOORIN \nO Helper (Who is) not helped, \nیَا شَاهِدًا غَیْرَ غَآئِبٍ\nYAA SHAAHEDAN GHAYRA GHAA-EBIN, \nO Present (Who is) not absent, \nیَا قَرِیْبًا غَیْرَ بَعِیْدٍ.\nYAA QAREEBAN GHAYRA BA-E’EDIN.\nO Near (Who is) not away.\n(47) To Cure Epilepsy\nیَا نُوْرَ النُّوْرِ یَا مُنَوِّرَ النُّوْرِ \nYAA NOORAN NOORE, YAA MOONAWWARAN NOORE, \nO Light and Light, O Illuminator of light, \nیَا خَالِقَ النُّوْرِ یَا مُدَبِّرَ النُّوْرِ \nYAA KHAALEQAN NOORE, YAA MODABBERAN NOORE, \nO Creator of light, O Director of Light, \nیَا مُقَدِّرًا النُّوْرِ یَا نُوْرَ كُلِّ نُوْرٍ \nYAA MOQADDERAN NOORE, YAA NOORA KULLE NOORIN, \nO Architect of light, O Light of every light, \nیَا نُوْرًا قَبْلَ كُلِّ نُوْرٍ یَا نُوْرًا بَعْدَ كُلِّ نُوْرٍ\nYAA NOORAN QABLA KULLE NOORIN, YAA NOORAN BA’DA KULLE NOORIN, \nO Light prior to every light, O Light beyond every light, \nیَا نُوْرًا فَوْقَ كُلِّ نُوْرٍ یَا نُوْرًا لَیْسَ كَمِثْلِهٖ نُوْرٌ.\nYAA NOORAN FAWQA KULLE NOORIN, YAA NOORAN LAYSA KAMISLEHI NOORUN.\nO Light superior to every light, O Light like of which there is no light.\n(48) To Get Rid Of Constipation\nیَا مَنْ عَطَآؤُهٗ شَرِیْفٌ یَا مَنْ فِعْلُهٗ لَطِیْفٌ \nYAA MAN A’TAA-OHU SHAREEFUN, YAA MAN FE’LOHU LATEEFUN, \nO He Whose gifts are excellent, O He Whose actions are subtle, \nیَا مَنْ لُطْفُهٗ مُقِیْمٌ یَا مَنْ اِحْسَانُهٗ قَدِیْمٌ\nYAA MAN LUTFOHU MOQIMUN, YAA MAN EHSANOHU QADEEMUN, \nO He Whose kindness is stable, O He Whose beneficence is eternal,\nیَا مَنْ قَوْلُهٗ حَقٌّ یَا مَنْ وَعْدُهٗ صِدْقٌ\nYAA MAN QAWLOHU HAQQUN, YAA MAN WA’DOHU SIDQOON, \nO He Whose word is true, O He Whose promise is sincere, \nیَا مَنْ عَفْوُهٗ فَضْلٌ یَا مَنْ عَذَابُهٗ عَدْلٌ\nYAA MAN A’FWOHU FAZLUN, YAA MAN A’ZAABOHU A’DLUN, \nO He Whose pardon is complete, O He Whose punishments is just, \nیَا مَنْ ذِكْرُهٗ حُلْوٌ یَا مَنْ فَضْلُهٗ عَمِیْمٌ.\nYAA MAN ZIKROHU HULVUN, YAA MAN FAZLOHU A’MEEMUN.\nO He Whose remembrance is pleasant, O He Whose bounties are for one and all. \n(49) To Cure Palpitation Of Heart\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا مُسَهِّلُ یَا مُفَصِّلُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA MOSAHHELO, YAA MOFAS-SELO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Simplifier, O Separator, \nیَا مُبَدِّلُ یَا مُذَلِّلُ یَا مُنَزِّلُ یَا مُنَوِّلُ\nYAA MOBADDELO, YAA MOZALLELO, YAA MONAZZELO, YAA MONAWWELO, \nO Compensator, O Tamer, O Hospitable, O Bestower of gifts, \nیَا مُفْضِلُ یَا مُجْزِلُ یَا مُمْهِلُ یَا مُجْمِلُ.\nYAA MUFZELO, YAA MUJZELO, YAA MUMHELO, YAA MUJMELO.\nO Bounteous, O Distributor, O Granter of respite, O Gatherer.\n(50) To Improve Eye Sight\nیَا مَنْ یَرٰی وَ لَا یُرٰی\nYAA MANY YARAA WA LA YORAA, \nO He Who sees but is not seen, \nیَا مَنْ یَّخْلُقُ وَ لَا یُخْلَقُ\nYAA MANY YAKHLOQO WA LAA YUKHLAQO, \nO He Who creates but is not created, \nیَا مَنْ یَّهْدِیْ وَ لَا یُهْدٰی\nYAA MANY YAHDE WA LAA YOHDAA \nO He Who guides but needs no guidance, \nیَا مَنْ یُّحْیِیْ وَ لَا یُحْیٰی\nYAA MANY YOHYEE WA LAA YOHYAA, \nO He Who animates but is not animated, \nیَا مَنْ یَّسْئَلُ وَ لَا یُسْئَلُ\nYAA MANY YAS-ALO WA LAA YUS-ALO \nO He Who calls to account but is not questioned, \nیَا مَنْ یُّطْعِمُ وَ لَا یُطْعَمُ\nYAA MANY YUT-E’MO WA LAA YUT-A’MO, \nO He Who gives to eat but does not eat, \nیَا مَنْ یُّجِیْرُ وَ لَا یُجَارُ عَلَیْهِ\nYAA MANY YOJEERO WA LAA YOJAARO A’LAYHE, \nO He Who gives protection but needs no protection \nیَا مَنْ یَّقْضِیْ وَ لَا یُقْضٰی عَلَیْهِ\nYAA MANY YAQZEE WA LAA YUQZAA A’LAYHE, \nO He Who adjudicates but is not judged, \nیَا مَنْ یَّحْكُمُ وَ لَا یُحْكَمُ عَلَیْهِ\nYAA MANY YAHKOMO WA LAA YOHKAMO A’LAYHE, \nO He Who rules but is not ruled, \nیَا مَنْ لَّمْ یَلِدْ وَ لَمْ یُوْ لَدْ وَ لَمْ یَكُنْ لَّهٗ كُفُوًا اَحَدٌ.\nYAA MAN LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD WA LAM YAKUL LAHU KOFOWAN AHAD.\nO He Who begets not nor was begotten; and there is none like Him.\n(51) To Dispel Mischief Of Enemy\nیَا نِعْمَ الْحَسِیْبُ یَا نِعْمَ الطَّبِیْبُ\nYAA NE’MAL HASEEBO, YAA NE’MAT TABEEBO, \nO Excellent Reckoner, O Excellent Doctor, \nیَا نِعْمَ الرَّقِیْبُ یَا نِعْمَ الْقَرِیْبُ\nYAA NE’MAR RAQEEBO, YAA NE’MAL QAREEBO, \nO Excellent Preserver, O Excellent Neighbour, \nیَا نِعْمَ الْمُجِیْبُ یَا نِعْمَ الْحَبِیْبُ\nYAA NE’MAL MOJEEBO, YAA NE’MAL HABEEBO, \nO Excellent Accepter, O Excellent Friend, \nیَا نِعْمَ الْكَفِیْلُ یَا نِعْمَ الْوَكِیْلُ\nYAA NE’MAL KAFEELO, YAA NE’MAL WAKEELO, \nO Excellent Assurer, O Excellent Advocate, \nیَا نِعْمَ الْمَوْلٰی یَا نِعْمَ النَّصِیْرُ.\nYAA NE’MAL MAWLAA YAA NE’MAN NASEERO.\nO Excellent Master, O Excellent Helper.\n(52) To Get Rid Of Poverty\nیَا سُرُوْرَ الْعَارِفِیْنَ یَا مُنَی الْمُحِبِّیْنَ \nYAA SOROORAL A’AREFEENA YAA MONAL MOHIBBEENA\nO Joy of the knowers, O Desire of the lovers, \nیَا اَنِیْسَ الْمُرِیْدِیْنَ یَا حَبِیْبَ التَّوَّابِیْنَ \nYAA ANEESAL MOREEDEENA YAA HABEEBAT TAWWAABEENA, \nO Companion of the devoted, O Friend of the repentant, \nیَا رَازِقَ الْمُقِلِّیْنَ یَا رَجَآءَ الْمُذْنِبِیْنَ \nYAA RAAZEQAL MOQILLEENA, YAA RAJAA-AL MUZNEBEENA, \nO provider of food to the have-nots, O Hope of the transgressors, \nیَا قُرَّۃَ عَیْنِ الْعَابِدِیْنَ یَا مُنَفِّسَ عَنِ الْمَكْرُوْبِیْنَ \nYAA QURRATA A’YNIL A’ABEDEENA, YAA MONAFFESA A’NIL MAKROOBEENA, \nO Apple of worshipper’s eyes, O Outlet for the sufferers, \nیَا مُفَرِّجَ عَنِ الْمَغْمُوْمِیْنَ یَا اِلٰهَ الْاَوَّلِیْنَ وَ الْاٰخِرِیْنَ.\nYAA MOFARREJA A’NIL MAGHMOOMEENA, YAA ELAAHAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHEREENA.\nO Comfort for the sorrowfuls, O God of the firsts and the lasts.\n(53) To Cultivate Love\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا رَبَّنَا یَا اِلٰهَنَا\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA, BISMEKA YAA RABBANAA, YAA ELAAHANAA,\nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O our Lord, O our God, \nیَا سَیِّدَنَا یَا مَوْلاَنَا یَا نَاصِرَنَا یَا حَافِظَنَا\nYAA SAYYEDANAA, YAA MAWLAANAA YAA NAASERANAA, YAA HAFEZANAA, \nO our Chief, O our Master, O our Helper, O our Guardian, \nیَا دَلِیْلَنَا یَا مُعِیْنَنَا یَا حَبِیْبَنَا یَا طَبِیْبَنَا.\nYAA DALEELANAA, YAA MO-E’ENANAA, YAA HABEEBANAA, YAA TABEEBANAA.\nO our Guide, O our Succourer, O our Friend, O our Doctor.\n(54) To Cure Toothache \nیَا رَبَّ النَّبِیِّیْنَ وَالْاَبْرَارِ یَا رَبَّ الصِّدِّیْقِیْنَ وَالْاَخْیَارِ \nYAA RABBAN NABIYYEENA WAL ABRAARE, YAA RABBAS SIDDEEQEENA WAL AKHYAARE, \nO Lord of the prophets and the pious, O Lord of the truthful and the righteous, \nیَا رَبَّ الْجَنَّۃِ وَالنَّارِ یَا رَبَّ الصِّغَارِ وَالْكِبَارِ \nYAA RABBAL JANNATE WAN NAARE, YAA RABBAS SEGHAARE, WAL KEBAARE, \nO Lord of paradise and hell, O Lord of the insignificant and the important, \nیَا رَبَّ الْحُبُوْبِ وَالثِّمَارِیَا رَبَّ الْاَنْهَارِ وَالْاَشْجَارِ \nYAA RABBAL HOBOOBE WAS SEMAARE, YAA RABBAL ANHAARE WAL ASHJAARE, \nO Lord of grain and fruit, O Lord of the rivers and the trees, \nیَا رَبَّ الصَّحَارِیْ وَالْقِفَارِ یَا رَبَّ الْبَرَارِیْ وَالْبِحَارِ \nYAA RABBAS SAHAAREE WAL QEFAARE, YAA RABBAL BARAAREE WAL BEHAARE, \nO Lord of the deserts and forests, O Lord of the lands and the seas, \nیَا رَبَّ اللَّیْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ یَا رَبَّ الْاَعْلاَنِ وَالْاَسْرَارِ.\nYAA RABBAL LAYLE WAN NAHAARE, YAA RABBAL E-A’LAANE WAL-ISRAARE.\nO Lord of the night and the day, O Lord of the apparent and the concealed.\n(55) To Cure Pain In Ribs \nیَا مَنْ نَّفَذَ فِیْ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ اَمْرُهٗ\nYAA MAN-NAFAZA FEE KULLE SHAY-IN AMROHU, \nO He Whose command controls everything, \nیَا مَنْ لَحِقَ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ عِلْمُهٗ\nYAA MAN LAHEQA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN I’LMOHU, \nO He Whose knowledge surrounds everything, \nیَا مَنْ بَلَغَتْ اِلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قُدْرَتُهٗ\nYAA MAN BALAGHAT ELAA KULLE SHAY-IN QUDRATOHU, \nO He Whose omnipotence overcomes everything, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا تُحْصِیْ الْعِبَادُ نِعَمَهٗ\nYAA MAN LAA TOHSIL E’BAADO NE-A’MAHU, \nO He Whose bounties cannot be counted by His servants, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا تَبْلُغُ الْخَلآئِقُ شُكْرَهٗ\nYAA MAN LAA TABLOGHUL KHALAA-E’QO SHUKRAHU, \nO He Whom the creatures cannot fully thank (as much as He is worthy of), \nیَا مَنْ لَّا تُدْرِكَ الْاَفْهَامُ جَلاَلَهٗ\nYAA MAN LAA TUDREKUL AFHAAMO JALAALAHU, \nO He Whose glory no intellect can grasp, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا تَنَالُ الْاَوْهَامُ كُنْهَهٗ\nYAA MAN LAA TANAALUL AW-HAAMO KUNHAHU, \nO He Whose real truth no imagination can make out, \nیَا مَنِ الْعَظَمَۃُ وَ الْكِبْرِیَآءُ رِدَآئُهٗ\nYAA MANIL A’ZAMATO WAL KIBREYAA-O REDAA-OHU, \nO He Whose cloak is majesty and greatness, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا تَرُدُّ الْعِبَادُ قَضَآئَهٗ\nYAA MAN LAA TARUDDUL E’BAADO QAZAA-AHU, \nO He Whose decree the servants cannot reject, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا مُلْكَ اِلَّا مُلْكُهٗ\nYAA MAN LAA MULKA ILLAA MULKAHU \nO He Who alone, and no one else, has the kingdom, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا عَطَآءَ اِلَّا عَطَآئُهٗ .\nYAA MAN LAA A’TAA-A ILLAA A’TAAOHU.\nO He Who alone, and no one else, bestows benefits.\n(56) To Cure Diseases\nیَا مَنْ لَّهُ الْمَثَلُ الْاَعْلٰی\nYAA MAN LAHUL MASALUL A-A’LAA, \nO He to Whom belong the highest examples, \nیَا مَنْ لَّهُ الصِّفَاتُ الْعُلْیَا\nYAA MAN LAHUS SEFAATUL U’LYAA \nO He to Whom belong the noblest qualities, \nیَا مَنْ لَّهُ الْاٰخِرَۃُ وَالْاُوْلٰی\nYAA MAN LAHUL AKHERATO WAL OOLAA,\nO He to Whom belong the beginning and the end, \nیَا مَنْ لَّهُ الْجَنَّۃُ الْمَاوٰی\nYAA MAN LAHUL JANNATUL MAAWAA \nO He to Whom belong the abodes of paradise, \nیَا مَنْ لَّهُ الْآیَاتُ الْكُبْرٰی\nYAA MAN LAHUL AAYAATUL KUBRAA, \nO He to Whom belong the great signs, \nیَا مَنْ لَّهُ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰی\nYAA MAN LAHUL ASMAAUL HUSNAA, \nO He to Whom belong the beautiful names, \nیَا مَنْ لَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَالْقَضَآءُ\nYAA MAN LAHUL HUKMO WAL QAZAAA-O, \nO He to Whom belong the command and the judgment, \nیَا مَنْ لَهُ الْهَوَآءُ وَالْفَضَآءُ\nYAA MAN LAHUL HAWAAA-O WAL-QAZAAA-O, \nO He to Whom belong the atmosphere and the space, \nیَا مَنْ لَهُ الْعَرْشُ وَ الثَّرٰی\nYAA MAN LAHUL A’RSHO WAS-SARAA, \nO He to Whom belong the throne and the ground, \nیَا مَنْ لَهُ السَّمٰوٰتُ الْعُلٰی.\nYAA MAN LAHUS-SAMAAWAATUL O’LAA.\nO He to Whom belong the high heavens.\n(57) To Prevent Hurricane\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا عَفُوُّ یَا غَفُوْرُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA A’FUWWO, YAA GHAFOORO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Sparer, O Remitter, \nیَا صَبُوْرُ یَا شَكُوْرُ یَا رَءُوْفُ یَا عَطُوْفُ\nYAA SABOORO, YAA SHAKOORO, YAA RA-O’OFO, YAA A’TOOFO, \nO Patient, O Thankful, O Compassionate, O Affectionate, \nیَا مَسْئُوْلُ یَا وَدُوْدُ یَا سُبُّوْحُ یَا قُدُّوْسُ.\nYAA MAS-OOLO, YAA WADOODO, YAA SUBBOOHO, YAA QUDDOOSO.\nO Besought, O Beloved, O Glorified, O Holy.\n(58) To Get Honour And Respect\nیَا مَنْ فِی السَّمَآءِ عَظَمَتُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIS-SAMAA-E A’ZAMATOHU, \nO He Whose greatness spreads in all directions of the heavens, \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْاَرْضِ اٰیَاتُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-ARZE AAYAATOHU, \nO He Whose signs are visible all over the earth, \nیَا مَنْ فِی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ دَلَآئِلُهٗ\nYAA MAN FEE KULLE SHAY-IN DALAALOHU, \nO He Whose arguments demonstrate through all objects, \nیَا مَنْ فِی الْبِحَارِ عَجَائِبُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-BEHAARE A’JAA-E’BOHU \nO He Whose wonders abound in the rivers and oceans, \nیَا مَنْ فِیْ الْجِبَالِ خَزَآئِنُهٗ\nYAA MAN FIL-JEBAALE KHAZAA-E’NOHU, \nO He Whose treasures are found in the mountains, \nیَا مَنْ یَّبْدَؤُ الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ یُعِیْدُهٗ\nYAA MANY YABDA-UL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOHU, \nO He Who starts the creation and thereupon repeats,\nیَا مَنْ اِلَیْهِ یَرْجِعُ الْاَمْرُ كُلُّهٗ\nYAA MAN ELAYHE YARJE-U’L AMRO KULLOHU \nO He to Whom are reverted all affairs, \nیَا مَنْ اَظْهَرَ فِی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ لُطْفَهٗ\nYAA MAN AZHARA FEE KULLE SHAY-IN LUTFOHU, \nO He Whose favours are evident in everything, \nیَا مَنْ اَحْسَنَ كُلَّ شَیْءٍ خَلْقَهٗ\nYAA MAN AHSANA KULLA SHAY-IN KHALQAHU, \nO He Who makes well whatever He creates, \nیَا مَنْ تَصَرَّفَ فِی الْخَلَآئِقِ قُدْرَتُهٗ.\nYAA MAN TASARRAFA FIL-KHALAA-EQE QUDRATOHU.\nO He Who manages His creation with authority.\n(59) To Cure Stomach-Ache\nیَا حَبِیْبَ مَنْ لَّا حَبِیْبَ لَهٗ\nYAA HABEEBA MAN LAA HABEEBA LAHU, \nO Friend of him who is friendless, \nیَا طَبِیْبَ مَنْ لَّا طَبِیْبَ لَهٗ\nYAA TABEEBA MAN LAA TABEEBA LAHU, \nO Curer of him who has no physician, \nیَا مُجِیْبَ مَنْ لَّا مُجِیْبَ لَهٗ\nYAA MOJEEBA MAN LAA MOJEEBA LAHU, \nO Answerer of him who has no responder, \nیَا شَفِیْقَ مَنْ لَّا شَفِیْقَ لَهٗ\nYAA SHAFEEQA MAN LAA SHAFEEQA LAHU, \nO Patron of him who has no sympathizer, \nیَا رَفِیْقَ مَنْ لَّا رَفِیْقَ لَهٗ\nYAA RAFEEQA MAN-LAA RAFIQA LAHU, \nO Companion of him who has no comrade, \nیَا مُغِیْثَ مَنْ لَّا مُغِیْثَ لَهٗ\nYAA MOGHEESA MAN LA MOGHEESA LAHU, \nO Helper of him who is helpless, \nیَا دَلِیْلَ مَنْ لَّا دَلِیْلَ لَهٗ\nYAA DALEELA MAN LAA DALEELA LAHU, \nO Guide of him who has no indication, \nیَا اَنِیْسَ مَنْ لَّا اَنِیْسَ لَهٗ\nYAA ANEESA MAN LAA ANEESA LAHU, \nO Confidant of him who has no associate, \nیَا رَاحِمَ مَنْ لَّا رَاحِمَ لَهٗ\nYAA RAAHEMA MAN LAA RAAHEMA LAHU, \nO Commiserator of him who has no pitier, \nیَا صَاحِبَ مَنْ لَّا صَاحِبَ لَهٗ.\nYAA SAAHEBA MAN LAA SAAHEBA LAHU.\nO Escort of him who has no colleague.\n(60) To Succeed In Vital Undertakings\nیَا كَافِیَ مَنِ اسْتَكْفَاهُ\nYAA KAAFEYA MANIS TAKFAAHO, \nO Satisfaction unto him who seeks His sufficiency, \nیَا هَادِیَ مَنِ اسْتَهْدَاهُ\nYAA HADEYA MANIS TAHDAAHO,\nO Guide unto him who is in need of His directions, \nیَا كَالِئَ مَنِ اسْتَكْلاَهُ \nYAA KAALEYA MANIS TAKLAAHO, \nO Surety unto him who looks for His protection, \nیَا رَاعِیَ مَنِ اسْتَرْعَاهُ \nYA RAA-E’YA MANIS TARA’AHO, \nO Custody unto him who requires His care, \nیَا شَافِیَ مَنِ اسْتَشْفَاهُ \nYAA SHAFEYA MANIS TASHFAAHO, \nO Cure unto him who asks for His treatment, \nیَا قَاضِیَ مَنِ اسْتَقْضَاهُ \nYAA QAAZEYA MANIS TAQZAAHO, \nO Judgement unto him who submits to His arbitration, \nیَا مُغْنِیَ مَنِ اسْتَغْنَاهُ \nYAA MOGHNEYA MANIS TAGHNAAHO, \nO Riches unto him who aspires for His abundance, \nیَا مُوْفِیَ مَنِ اسْتَوْفَاهُ \nYAA MOOFIYA MANIS TAWFAAHO \nO Fulfillment unto him who calls for His attention, \nیَا مُقَوِّیَ مَنِ اسْتَقْوَاهُ \nYAA MOQAWWEYA MANIS TAQWAAHO, \nO Strength unto him who solicits for His tenacity, \nیَا وَلِیَّ مَنِ اسْتَوْلاَهُ.\nYAA WALIYYA MANIS TAWLAAHO.\nO Patron unto him who looks up for His favours.\n(61) To Seek Tranquility\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا خَالِقُ یَا رَازِقُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA KHAALEQO, YAA RAAZEQO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Creator, O Giver of livelihood, \nیَا نَاطِقُ یَا صَادِقُ یَا فَالِقُ یَا فَارِقُ \nYAA NAATEQO, YAA SAADEQO, YAA FAALEQO, YAA FAAREQO, \nO Rational, O Truthful, O Splitter, O Distinguisher, \nیَا فَاتِقُ یَا رَاتِقُ یَا سَابِقُ یَا سَامِقُ.\nYAA FAATEQO, YAA RAATEQO, YAA SAABEQO, YAA SAAMEQO.\nO Separator, O Restorer, O Foremost, O High.\n(62) To Win Friendship Of The Rich\nیَا مَنْ یُّقَلِّبُ اللَّیْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ\nYAA MAN YOQALLEBUL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA, \nO He Who interchanges night and day, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ الظُّلُمَاتِ وَالْاَنْوَارَ\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAZ ZOLOMAATA WAL-ANWAARA, \nO He Who created light and darkness, \nیَا مَنْ خَلَقَ الظِّلَ وَالْحَرُوْرَ\nYAA MAN KHALAQAZ ZILLA WAL-HAROORA, \nO He Who created shade and warmth, \nیَا مَنْ سَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ\nYAA MAN SAKH-KHARASH SHAMSA WAL-QAMARA, \nO He Who keeps in line the sun and the moon, \nیَا مَنْ قَدَّرَ الْخَیْرَ وَالشَّرَّ\nYAA MAN QADDARAL KHAYRA WASH SHARRA, \nO He Who takes account of good and evil, \nیَا مَنْ خَلَقَ الْمَوْتَ وَالْحَیٰوۃَ\nYAA MAN KHALAQAL MAWTA WAL-HAYAATA, \nO He Who brings about life and death, \nیَا مَنْ لَّهُ الْخَلْقُ وَالْاَمْرُ\nYAA MAN LAHUL KHALQO WAL-AMRO, \nO He to Whom belong creation and command, \nیَا مَنْ لَّمْ یَتَّخِذْ صَاحِبَۃً وَّ لَا وَلَدًا\nYAA MAN LAM YAT-TAKHIZ SAAHEBATAWN WA LAA WALADAN, \nO He Who does not take up wife or child, \nیَا مَنْ لَیْسَ لَهٗ شَرِیْكٌ فِی الْمُلْكِ\nYAA MAN LAYSA LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL-MULKE, \nO He Who shares with no one in exercise of authority, \nیَا مَنْ لَّمْ یَكُنْ لَّهٗ وَلِیٌّ مِنَ الذُّلِّ.\nYAA MAN LAM YAKUN-LAHU WALIYYUM MENAZ ZULLE.\nO He Who does not choose friend from among the vulgar.\n(63) To Make Profit In Business\nیَا مَنْ یَّعْلَمُ مُرَادَ الْمُرِیْدِیْنَ\nYAA MANY YA’LAMO MORAADAL MOREEDEENA, \nO He Who is aware of the desire of the hopeful, \nیَا مَنْ یَّعْلَمُ ضَمِیْرَ الصَّامِتِیْنَ\nYAA MANY YA’LAMO ZAMEERAS SAAMETEENA, \nO He Who is aware of the mind of the silent, \nیَا مَنْ یَّسْمَعُ اَنِیْنَ الْوَاهِنِیْنَ\nYAA MANY YASMA-O ANEENAL WAAHENEENA, \nO He Who hears the groanings of the weak, \nیَا مَنْ یَّرٰی بُكَآءَ الْخَآئِفِیْنَ\nYAA MANY YARAA BOKAA-AL KHAA-EFEENA, \nO He Who takes notice of the crying of the afraid, \nیَا مَنْ یَّمْلِكُ حَوَآئِجَ السَّآئِلِیْنَ\nYAA MANY YAMLEKO HAWAA-EJAS SAA-ELEENA, \nO He Who meets the demands of the needy, \nیَا مَنْ یَقْبَلُ عُذْرَ التَّآئِبِیْنَ\nYAA MANY YAQBALO OOZRAT TAA-EBEENA, \nO He Who accepts the excuse of the repentant, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یُصْلِحُ اَعْمَالَ الْمُفْسِدِیْنَ\nYAA MAN LAA YUSLEHO A’MALAL MUFSEDEENA, \nO He Who does not make better the ways of the mischievous, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یُضِیْعَ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِیْنَ\nYAA MAN LAA YOZEE-O AJRAL MOHSENEENA \nO He Who does not let go waste the reward of the praiseworthy, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یَبْعُدُ عَنْ قُلُوْبِ الْعَارِفِیْنَ\nYAA MAN LAA YAB-O’DO A’N QOLOOBIL A’AREFEENA, \nO He Who is not far away from the hearts of the intelligent, \nیَا اَجْوَدَ الْاَجْوَدِیْنَ.\nYAA AJWADAL AJWADEENA.\nO The Most Generous of all generous.\n(64) To Cure Splitting Headache\nیَا دَآئِمَ الْبَقَآءِ یَا سَامِعَ الدُّعَآءِ\nYAA DAA-E’MAL BAQAA-E, YAA SAAME-A’D DOAA-E, \nO Continuous Ever-lasting, O Listener of invocations,\nیَا وَاسِعَ الْعَطَاءِ یَا غَافِرَ الْخَطَآءِ\nYAA WAASE-A’L ATAA-E, YAA GAAFERAL KHATAAYAA \nO Liberal Bestower, O Absolver of transgressions, \nیَا بَدِیْعَ السَّمَاءِ یَا حَسَنَ الْبَلَآءِ\nYAA BADI-A’S SAMAA-E, YAA HUSNAL BALAA-E, \nO Establisher of sky, O Skilful Tester, \nیَا جَمِیْلَ الثَّنَآءِ یَا قَدِیْمَ السَّنَآءِ\nYAA JAMEELAS SANAA-E, YAA QADEEMAS SANAA-E, \nO Excellent Praiser, O Eternally Sublime, \nیَا كَثِیْرَ الْوَفَآءِ یَا شَرِیْفَ الْجَزَآءِ.\nYAA KASEERAL WAFAA-E, YAA SHAREEFAL JAZAA-E.\nO Liberal Fulfiller, O Noble Rewarder.\n(65) To Seek Forgiveness Of Sins\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا سَتَّارُ یَا غَفَّارُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA SATTAARO YAA GHAFFAARO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O very Forgiving, O Who covers (sins), \nیَا قَهَّارُ یَا جَبَّارُ یَا صَبَّارُ یَا بَآرُّ\nYAA QAHHAARO, YAA JABBAARO, YAA SABBAARO, YAA BAARRO \nO Who wields power, O Who puts in force (laws) O Who endures calmly, O Who acts well, \nیَا مُخْتَارُ یَا فَتَّاحُ یَا نَفَّاحُ یَا مُرْتَاحُ.\nYAA MUKHTAARO, YAA FATTAAHO, YAA NAFFAAHO, YAA MURTAAHO.\nO Who exercises free will, O Who takes into possession, O Who moves (winds), O Who gives comfort.\n(66) To Get Rid Of Poverty\nیَا مَنْ خَلَقَنِیْ وَ سَوَّانِیْ یَا مَنْ رَزَقَنِیْ وَ رَبَّانِیْ\nYAA MAN KHALAQANEE WA SAWWAANEE, YAA MAN RAZAQANEE WA RABBAANEE, \nO He Who created me and shaped me well, O He Who gave sustenance and put me in good order, \nیَا مَنْ اَطْعَمَنِیْ وَ سَقَانِیْ یَا مَنْ قَرَّبَنِیْ وَ اَدْنَانِیْ\nYAA MAN AT-A’MANEE WA SAQAANEE, YAA MAN QARRABANEE WA ADNAANEE, \nO He Who fed me and arranged water for me, O He Who kept me near and gave me wisdom, \nیَا مَنْ عَصَمَنِیْ وَ كَفَانِیْ یَا مَنْ حَفَظَنِیْ وَ كَلَانِیْ\nYAA MAN A’SAMANEE WA KAFAANEE, YAA MAN HAFAZANEE WA KALAANEE, \nO He Who preserved me and defended me, O He Who protected me and kept me safe, \nیَا مَنْ اَعَزَّنِیْ وَ اَغْنَانِیْ یَا مَنْ وَفَّقَنِیْ وَ هَدَانِیْ\nYAA MAN A-A’ZZANEE WA AGHNAANEE, YAA MAN WAQAFANEE WA HADAANEE, \nO He Who paid attention to me and made me well-to-do, O He Who perfected me and showed me the right path, \nیَا مَنْ اٰنَسَنِیْ وَ اٰوَانِیْ یَا مَنْ اَمَاتَنِیْ وَ اَحْیَانِیْ.\nYAA MAN AANASANEE WA AAWAANEE, YAA MAN AMAATANEE WA AHYAANEE.\nO He Who became familiar with me and received me gladly, O He Who puts me to death and brings me to life.\n(67) To Cure Eye Ailments\nیَا مَنْ یُّحِقُّ الْحَقَّ بِكَلِمَاتِهٖ\nYAA MANY YOHIQQUL HAQQA BE-KALEMAATEHI, \nO He Who confirms truth by His words, \nیَا مَنْ یَّقْبَلُ التَّوْبَۃَ عَنْ عِبَادِهٖ\nYAA MANY YAQBALAT TAWBATA A’N E’BAADEHI, \nO He Who corresponds to the repentance of his servants of His servants, \nیَا مَنْ یَّحُوْلُ بَیْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَ قَلْبِهٖ\nYAA MANY YAHOOLO BAYNAL MAR-E WA QALBEHI, \nO He Who intervenes between man and his soul, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا تَنْفَعُ الشَّفَاعَۃُ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِهٖ\nYAA MAN LAA TANFA-O’SH SHAFAA-A’TA ILLAA BE-IZNEHI, \nO He Who does not take notice of any intercession unless by His leave, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ ضَلَّ عَنْ سَبِیْلِهٖ\nYAA MAN HOWA A’LAMO BE-MAN ZALLA A’N SABEELEHI,\nO He Who is well aware of him who abandons the right path and goes astray, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا مُعَقِّبَ لِحُكْمِهٖ\nYAA MAN-LA MO’AQ-QEBA LE-HUKMEHI, \nO He Whose command no one can criticize, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا رَآدَّ لِقَضَآئِهٖ\nYAA MAN-LAA RAADDAA LE-QAZAA-EHI, \nO He Whose proclamation no one can revoke, \nیَا مَنِ انْقَادَ كُلُّ شَیْءٍ لِّاَمْرِهٖ\nYAA MANIN QAADA KULLO SHAY-IN LE-AMREHI, \nO He Whose Directions everyone follows, \nیَا مَنِ السَّمٰوٰتُ مَطْوِیَّاتٌ بِیَمِیْنِهٖ\nYAA MANIS-SAMAAWAATO MATWIYYAATUN BE-YAMEENEHI, \nO He under Whose control the skies extend across, \nیَا مَنْ یُّرْسِلُ الرِّیَاحَ بُشْرًا بَیْنَ یَدَیْ رَحْمَتِهٖ.\nYAA MANY YURSELUR REYAAHA BUSHRAN BAYNA YADAY RAHMATEHI.\nO He Who sends winds as harbinger of glad-tidings through His mercy.\n(68) To Ward Off Plague\nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ الْاَرْضَ مِهَادًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAL ARZA MEHAADAN, \nO He Who has made the earth like a spread out surface,\nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ الْجِبَالَ اَوْتَادًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAL JEBAALA AWTADAN,\nO He Who has rammed in the mountains like pegs, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ الشَّمْسَ سِرَاجًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LASH SHAMSA SERAAJAN, \nO He Who has adorned the sun like a chandelier, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ الْقَمَرَ نُوْرًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAL QAMARA NOORAN, \nO He Who has lit up to moon like a luminary, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ اللَّیْلَ لِبَاسًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAL LAYLA LEBAASAN, \nO He Who has created the night as a covering,\nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ النَّهَارَ مَعَاشًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAN NAHAARA MA-A’ASHAN, \nO He Who has created the day to act and procure livelihood, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ النَّوْمَ سُبَاتًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAN NAWMA SOBAATAN, \nO He Who has appointed the sleep for rest, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ السَّمَآءَ بِنَآءً\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAS SAMAA-A BENAA-AN, \nO He Who has established the sky like an arch, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ الْاَشْیَآءَ اَزْوَاجًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAL ASHYAA-A AZWAAJAN \nO He Who has created pairs of all kind (of living creatures), \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ النَّارَ مِرْصَادًا.\nYAA MAN JA-ALAN NAARA MIRSAADAN.\nO He Who has made Hell an ambush (for infidels).\n(69) To Achieve Eminence\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا سَمِیْعُ یَا شَفِیْعُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA SAMEE-O YAA SHAFEE-O’,\nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Who hears, O Who accepts intercession \nیَا رَفِیْعُ یَا مَنِیْعُ یَا سَرِیْعُ یَا بَدِیْعُ\nYAA RAFEE-O’, YAA MANEE-O’, YAA SAREE-O’, YAA BADEE-O’, \nO Who bestows ranks, O Who prohibits, O Who is swift, O Who originates, \nیَا كَبِیْرُ یَا قَدِیْرُ یَا خَبِیْرُ یَا مُجِیْرُ.\nYAA KABEERO, YAA QADEERO, YAA KHABEERO, YAA MOJEERO.\nO Who is powerful O Who is omnipotent, O Who is well-informed, O Who gives support.\n(70) To Get Long Life\nیَا حَیًّا قَبْلَ كُلِّ حَیٍّ یَا حَیًّا بَعْدَ كُلِّ حَیٍّ\nYAA HAYYAN QABLA KULLE HAYYIN, YAA HAYYAN BA’DA KULLE HAYYIN \nO (uncaused) Living, ahead of all life, O Alive (eternally), beyond all life, \nیَا حَیُّ الَّذِیْ لَیْسَ كَمِثْلِهٖ حَیٌّ یَا حَیُّ الَّذِیْ لَا یُشَارِكُهٗ حَیٌّ\nYAA HAYYUL LAZEE LAYSA KAMISLEHI HAYYUN, YAA HAYYOOL LAZEE LAYSA YOSHAAREKOHU HAYYUN, \nO (Ever) Living like unto Whom there is no being, O (Ever) Living with Whom no (kept alive) partner is associated, \nیَا حَیُّ الَّذِیْ لَا یَحْتَاجُ اِلٰی حَیٍّ یَا حَیُّ الَّذِیْ یُمِیْتُ كُلَّ حَیٍّ\nYAA HAYYUL LAZEE LAA YAHTAAJO ILLA HAYYIN, YAA HAYYUL LAZEE YOMEETO KULLA HAYYIN, \nO (Ever) Living Who turns not to any (kept alive) being, O (Ever) Living Who puts every living being to death, \nیَا حَیُّ الَّذِیْ یَرْزُقُ كُلَّ حَیٍّ یَا حَیًّا لَمْ یَرِثِ الْحَیٰوۃَ مِنْ حَيٍّ\nYAA HAYYUL-LAZEE YARZOQO KULLA HAYYIN, YAA HAYYAN LAM YARESIL HAYAATA MIN HAYYIN, \nO (Ever) Living Who did not receive life from any being, O (Ever) Living Who gives livelihood to all living beings, \nیَا حَیُّ الَّذِیْ یُحْیِ الْمَوْتٰی یَا حَیُّ یَا قَیُّوْمُ لَا تَاْخُذُهٗ سِنَۃٌ وَّلاَ نَوْمٌ.\nYAA HAYYUL LAZEE YOHYIL MAWTA YAA HAYYO, YAA QAYYOOMO LA TAAKHOZOHU SENATUN WA LAA NAWM.\nO (Ever) Living Who has kept death operative, O (Ever) Living, O Ever-Lasting, Slumber seizes Him not, nor sleep.\n(71) To Prevent Cyclone\nیَا مَنْ لَهٗ ذِكْرٌ لَا یُنْسٰی یَا مَنْ لَهٗ نُوْرٌ لَا یُطْفٰی\nYAA MAN LAHU ZIKRUN LAA YUNSAA YAA MAN LAHU NOORUN LAA YUTFAA, \nO He Whose mention (name) is never put off, O He Whose Light is never extinguished,\nیَا مَنْ لَهٗ نِعَمٌ لَا تُعَدُّ یَا مَنْ لَهٗ مُلْكٌ لَا یَزُوْلُ\nYAA MAN LAHU NE’AMUL LAA TOA’DDO, YAA MAN LAHU MULKUN LAA YAZOOLO, \nO He Whose bounties are countless, O He Whose kingdom does not wither away, \nیَا مَنْ لَهٗ ثَنَآءٌ لَا یُحْصٰی یَا مَنْ لَهٗ جَلَالٌ لَا یُكَیَّفُ\nYAA MAN LAHU SANAA-U’L LAA YOHSAA, YAA MAN LAHU JALAALUL LAA YOKAYYAFO, \nO He Whose praise knows no bounds, O He Whose power never diminishes, \nیَا مَنْ لَهٗ كَمَالٌ لَا یُدْرَكُ یَا مَنْ لَهٗ قَضَآءٌ لَا یُرَدُّ\nYAA MAN LAHU KAMALUL LAA YUDRAKO, YAA MAN LAHU QAZAA-UL LAA YORADDO, \nO He Whose perfection is unperceivable, O He Whose decree is irrevocable, \nیَا مَنْ لَهٗ صِفَاتٌ لَا تُبَدَّلُ یَا مَنْ لَهٗ نُعُوْتٌ لَا تُغَیَّرُ.\nYAA MAN LAHU SEFAATUL LAA TOBADDALO, YAA MAN LAHU NO-O’OTUN LAA TOGHAYYARO.\nO He Whose attributes are not transposable, O He Whose praise never loses colour.\n(72) To Cure Pain In Breasts\nیَا رَبَّ الْعٰلَمِیْنَ یَا مَالِكَ یَوْمِ الدِّیْنَ\nYAA RABBAL A’ALAMEENA, YAA MAALEKA YAWMIDDEENE, \nO Lord of the worlds, O Owner of the Day of Judgement, \nیَا غَایَۃَ الطَّالِبِیْنَ یَا ظَهْرَ اللَّاجِیْنَ\nYAA GHAAYATAT TAALEBEENA, YAA ZAHRAL LAAJEENA, \nO Last Resort of those who strive for, O Support of those who have plunged into the deep, \nیَا مُدْرِكَ الْهَارِبِیْنَ یَا مَنْ یُّحِبُّ الصَّابِرِیْنَ\nYAA MUDREKAL HAAREBEENA, YAA MANY YOHIBBUS SAABEREENA, \nO Seizer of fugitives, O He Who loves those who endure without complaints, \nیَا مَنْ یُّحِبُّ التَّوَّابِیْنَ یَا مَنْ یُّحِبُّ الْمُتَطَهِّرِیْنَ\nYAA MANY YOHIBBUT TAWWAABEENA, YAA MANY YOHIBBUL MOTATAHHEREENA, \nO He Who loves the repentants, O He Who loves the pure, \nیَا مَنْ یُّحِبُّ الْمَحْسِنِیْنَ یَا مَنْ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِیْنَ.\nYAA MANY YOHIBBUL MOHSENEENA, YAA MAN HOWA A’LAMO BIL-MOHTADEENA.\nO He Who loves the good, O He Who knows best about those who are on the right path.\n(73) To Cure Rheumatism\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا شَفِیْقُ یَا رَفِیْقُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA, YAA SHAFEEQO, YAA RAFEEQO,\nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Solicitous, O Kind Friend, O Administrator,\nیَا حَفِیْظُ یَا مُحِیْطُ یَا مُقِیْتُ یَا مُغِیْثُ \nYAA HAFEEZO, YAA MOHEETO, YAA MOQEETO, YAA MOGHEESO, \nO Who surrounds, O Who gives sustenance, O Who comes to help, O Who confers honour, \nیَا مُعِزُّ یَا مُذِلُّ یَا مُبْدِءُ یَا مُعِیْدُ.\nYAA MO-I’ZZO, YAA MOZILLO, YAA MUBDE’O, YAA MO-E’EDO.\nO Who subdues, O Who begins, O Who brings back.\n(74) To Have A Son\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ اَحَدٌ بِلَا ضِدٍّ یَا مَنْ هُوَ فَرْدٌ بِلَا نِدٍّ\nYAA MAN HOWA AHADUN BELAA ZIDDIN, YAA MAN HOWA FARDUN BELA NIDDIN, \nO He Who is single without a counterpart, O He Who is one without a rival, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ صَمَدٌ بِلَا عَیْبٍ یَا مَنْ هُوَ وِتْرٌ بِلَا كَیْفٍ\nYAA MAN HOWA SAMADUN BELAA A’YBIN, YAA MAN HOWA VITRUN BELAA KAYFIN, \nO He Who is free from all wants without a defect, O He Who is one and only without chaos, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ قَاضٍ بِلَا حَیْفٍ یَا مَنْ هُوَ رَبٌّ بِلَا وَزِیْرِ\nYAA MAN HOWA QAAZIN BELAA HAYFIN, YAA MAN HOWA RABBUN BELAA WAZEERIN, \nO He Who settles matters without oppression, O He Who rules without an assistant, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ عَزِیْزٌ بِلَا ذُلٍّ یَا مَنْ هُوَ غَنِیٌّ بِلَا فَقْرٍ\nYAA MAN HOWA A’ZEEZUN BELAA ZULLIN, YAA MAN HOWA GHANIYYUN BELAA FAQEERIN, \nO He Who is glorious without humiliation, O He Who is self-sufficient without privation, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ مَلِكٌ بِلَا عَزْلٍ یَا مَنْ هُوَ مَوْصُوْفٌ بِلَا شَبِیْهٍ.\nYAA MAN HOWA MALAKUN BELAA A’ZLIN, YAA MAN HOWA MAWSOOFUN BELAA SHABEEHIN.\nO He Who masters without degrading (His Servants), O He Whose attributes are described without ascribing similarities.\n(75) To Achieve Honourable Position\nیَا مَنْ ذِكْرُهٗ شَرَفٌ لِّلذَّاكِرِیْنَ\nYAA MAN ZIKROHU SHARAFUN LIZ-ZAAKEREENA, \nO He remembrance of Whom gives distinction to the rememberers, \nیَا مَنْ شُكْرُهٗ فَوْزٌ لِّلشَّاكِرِیْنَ\nYAA MAN SHUKROHU FAWZOON LISH-SHAAKEREENA, \nO He thankfulness unto Whom renders the thankful successful, \nیَا مَنْ حَمْدُهٗ عِزٌّ لِّلْحَامِدِیْنَ\nYAA MAN HAMDOHU I’ZZUN LIL-HAAMEDEENA, \nO He praise of Whom gives honour to the praisers, \nیَا مَنْ طَاعَتُهٗ نَجَاۃٌ لِّلْمُطِیْعِیْنَ\nYAA MAN TA-A’TOHU NAJAATUN LIL-MOTEE-E’ENA, \nO He obedience unto Whom delivers the obedient, \nیَا مَنْ بَابُهٗ مَفْتُوْحٌ لِّلْطَّالِبِیْنَ\nYAA MAN BAABOHU MAFTOOHUN LIT-TAALEBEENA,\nO He Whose door is kept open for the beseechers, \nیَا مَنْ سَبِیْلُهٗ وَاضِحٌ لِّلْمُنِیْبِیْنَ\nYAA MAN SABEELOHU WAAZEHUN LIL-MONEEBEENA, \nO He Whose path is evident to those who turn to (Him), \nیَا مَنْ اٰیَاتُهٗ بُرْهَانٌ لِّلنَّاظِرِیْنَ\nYAA MAN AAYAATOHU BURHANUN LIN-NAAZEREENA,\nO He Whose signs are arguments for those who look into, \nیَا مَنْ كِتَابُهٗ تَذْكِرَۃٌ لِّلْمُتَّقِیْنَ\nYAA MAN KETAABOHU TAZKERATUN LIL-MUTTAQEENA, \nO He Whose Book (Holy Quran) is the conversation of the pious, \nیَا مَنْ رِّزْقُهٗ عُمُومٌ لِّلطَّآئِعِیْنَ وَالْعَاصِیْنَ\nYAA MAN-RIZQOHU O’MOOMUN LIT-TAA-E-E’ENA WAL A’ASEENA,\nO He Who gives livelihood in general to the disobedient as good as to the obedient, \nیَا مَنْ رَّحْمَتُهٗ قَرِیْبٌ مِّنَ الْمُحْسِنِیْنَ.\nYAA MAN RAHMATOHU QAREEBUN MENAL MOHSENEENA.\nO He Whose mercy is near at hand to the virtuous.\n(76) To Cure Leprosy\nیَا مَنْ تَبَارَكَ اسْمُهٗ یَا مَنْ تَعَالٰی جَدُّهٗ \nYAA MAN TABAARAKASMOHU, YAA MAN TA-A’ALA JADDOHU, \nO He Whose name brings blessings in abundance, O He Whose nobility is praiseworthy, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا اِلٰهَ غَیْرُهٗ یَا مَنْ جَلَّ ثَنَآؤُهٗ \nYAA MAN LAA ELAAHA GHAYROHU, YAA MAN JALLA SANAA-OHU, \nO He other than Who there is no god, O He Whose praise is glorious, \nیَا مَنْ تَقَدَّسَتْ اَسْمَآؤُهٗ یَا مَنْ یَّدُوْمُ بَقَآؤُهٗ \nYAA MAN TAQADDASAT ASMAA-OHU, YAA MANY-YADOOMO BAQAA-OHU, \nO He Whose names are holy, O He Whose continuance is ever-lasting, \nیَا مَنِ الْعَظَمَۃُ بَهَآؤُهٗ یَا مَنِ الْكِبْرِیَآءُ رِدَآؤُهٗ \nYAA MANIL A’ZAMATO BAHAA-OHU, YAA MANIL KIBREYAA-O REDAA-OHU \nO He Whose brilliance Is extensive, O He Whose pride is His companion, \nیَا مَنْ لَا تُحْصٰی اٰلَآؤُهٗ یَا مَنْ لَا تُعَدُّ نَعْمَآؤُهٗ.\nYAA MAN LAA TOHSAA AALAA-OHU YAA MAN LAA TO-A’DDO NA’MAAOHU.\nO He summing up of Whose bestowals is not possible, O He Whose innumerable bounties are countless.\n(77) To Liquidate Debts\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا مُعِیْنُ یَا اَمِیْنُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA MO-E’ENO, YAA AMEENO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Who lends a hand, O Trustworthy, \nیَا مُبِیْنُ یَا مَتِیْنُ یَا مَكِیْنُ یَا رَشِیْدُ\nYAA MOBEENO, YA MATEENO, YAA MAKEENO YAA RASHEEDO, \nO Distinct, O Persevering, O Permanently Established, O Who guides well, \nیَا حَمِیْدُ یَا مَجِیْدُ یَا شَدِیْدُ یَا شَهِیْدُ.\nYAA HAMEEDO, YAA MAJEEDO, YAA SHADEEDO, YAA SHAHEEDO.\nO Praiseworthy, O Celebrated, O Severe, O Witness.\n(78) To Receive Love And Affection\nیَا ذَا الْعَرْشِ الْمَجِیْدِ یَا ذَا الْقَوْلِ السَّدِیْدِ\nYAA ZAL A’RSHIL MAJEEDE, YAA ZAL QAWLIS SADEEDE, \nO Lord of the glorious throne, O Lord of truthful words, \nیَا ذَا الْفِعْلِ الرَّشِیْدِ یَا ذَا البَطْشِ الشَّدِیْدِ\nYAA ZAL FE’LIR RASHEEDE, YAA ZAL BATSHISH SHADEED, \nO Lord of deeds and guidance, O Hard Taskmaster, \nیَا ذَا الْوَعْدِ وَالْوَعِیْدِ یَا مَنْ هُوَ الْوَلِیُّ الْحَمِیْدُ\nYAA ZAL WA’DE WAL-WA-E’EDE, YAA MAN HOWAL WALIYYUL HAMEEDO, \nO Lord of hope and fear, O He Who is a praiseworthy friend,\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فَعَّالٌ لِّمَا یُرِیْدُ یَا مَنْ هُوَ قَرِیْبٌ غَیْرُ بَعِیْدٍ\nYAA MAN HOWA FA-A’ALUL LEMAA YOREEDO, YAA MAN HOWA QAREEBUN GHAYRA BA-E’EDIN, \nO He Who does whatever He wills, O He Who is near, not far, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ شَهِیْدٌ یَا مَنْ هُوَ لَیْسَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِیْدِ.\nYAA MAN HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEEDUN, YAA MAN HOWA LAYSA BE-ZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEEDE.\nO He Who is a witness over all things, O He Who does not oppress His servants.\n(79) To Seek Freedom From Imprisonment\nیَا مَنْ لَّا شَرِیْكَ لَهٗ وَ لَا وَزِیْرَ\nYAA MAN LAA SHAREEKA LAHU WA LAA WAZEERA, \nO He Who shares not with a partner, nor takes up an assistant, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا شَبِیْهَ لَهٗ وَ لَا نَظِیْرَ\nYAA MAN LAA SHABEEHA LAHU WA LAA NAZEERA, \nO He unto Whom there is no likeness, nor analogy, \nیَا خَالِقَ الشَّمْسِ وَالْقَمَرِ الْمُنِیْرِ\nYAA KHALEQASH SHAMSE WAL-QAMARIL MONEERE,\nO Creator of the sun and the bright moon, \nیَا مُغْنِیَ الْبَآئِسِ الْفَقِیْرِ\nYAA MUGHNEYAL BAA-E’SIL-FAQEERE \nO Who makes the listless poor rich, \nیَا رَازِقَ الطِّفْلِ الصَّغِیْرِ\nYAA RAAZEKAT TIFLIS SAGHEERE, \nO Who arranges food for the just born baby, \nیَا رَاحِمَ الشَّیْخِ الْكَبِیْرِ\nYAA RAAHEMASH SHAYKHIL KABEERE, \nO Who takes care of the old age, \nیَا جَابِرَ الْعَظْمِ الْكَسِیْرِ \nYAA JAABERAL A’ZMIL KASEERE, \nO Who sets broken bones, \nیَا عِصْمَۃَ الْخَآئِفِ الْمُسْتَجِیْرِ \nYAA I’SMATAL KHAA-E’FIL MUSTAJEERE, \nO Who keeps watch over the afraid peti-tioners, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِیْرٌ بَصِیْرٌ \nYAA MAN HOWA BE-EBAADEHI KHABEERUN BASEEROON, \nO He Who is All-Knowing and All-Seeing towards His servants, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ.\nYAA MAN HOWA A’LA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN.\nO He Who wields absolute power over all things.\n(80) To Seek Prosperity\nیَا ذَا الْجُوْدِ وَالنِّعَمِ یَا ذَا الْفَضْلِ وَالْكَرَمِ \nYAA ZAL JOODE WAN-NE-A’ME, YAA ZAL FAZLE WAL-KARAME, \nO Lord of plenty and comforts, O Lord of super abundance and generosity, \nیَا خَالِقَ اللَّوْحِ وَالْقَلَمِ یَا بَارِءَ الذَّرِّ وَالنَّسَمِ \nYAA KHAALEQAL LAWHE WAL-QALAME, YAA BAARE-AZ ZARRE WAN-NASAME, \nO Creator of Lawh (smooth surfaced material to write) and Qalam (pen), O Who created ants and human beings, \nیَا ذَا الْبَاْسِ وَالنِّقَمِ یَا مُلْهِمَ الْعَرَبِ وَالْعَجَمِ \nYAA ZAL BAASE WAN-NEQAME, YAA MULHEMAL A’RABE WAL A’JAME,\nO Lord of power and punishment, O who inspires Arabs and non-Arabs, \nیَا كَاشِفَ الضُّرِّ وَالْاَلَمِ یَا عَالِمَ السِّرِّ وَالْهِمَمِ \nYAA KASHEFAZ ZURRE WAL-ALAME, YAA A’ALEMAS SIRRE WAL-HEMAME, \nO Disperser of Hardships and sorrows, O Knower of secrets and intentions, \nیَا رَبَّ الْبَیْتِ وَالْحَرَمِ یَا مَنْ خَلَقَ الْاَشْیَآءَ مِنَ الْعَدَمِ.\nYAA RABBAL BAYTE WAL-HARAME, YAA MAN KHALAQAL ASHYAA-A MENAL A’DAME.\nO Lord of the House and the sacred precinct (Holy Kaabah and its surroundings), O He Who brought forth things from the unknown.\n(81) To Cure Migraine\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا فَاعِلُ یَا جَاعِلُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA, BISMEKA, YAA FAA-E’LO, YAA JAA-E’LO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Executor, O Maker, \nیَا قَابِلُ یَا كَامِلُ یَا فَاصِلُ یَا وَاصِلُ\nYAA QAABELO, YAA KAAMELO, YAA FAASELO, YAA FAAZELO \nO Receiver, O Complete, O Cultivated, O Uniter, \nیَا عَادِلُ یَا غَالِبُ یَا طَالِبُ یَا وَاهِبُ.\nYAA A’ADELO, YAA GHALEBO, YAA TAALEBO, YAA WAAHEBO.\nO Just, O Who overcomes, O Who demands, O Who gives gifts.\n(82) To Cure Ulcer\nیَا مَنْ اَنْعَمَ بِطَوْلِهٖ یَا مَنْ اَكْرَمَ بِجُوْدِهٖ\nYAA MAN AN-A’MA BE-TAWLEHI, YAA MAN AKRAMA BE-JOODEHI,\nO He Who gives long lasting rewards, O He Who is abundantly generous, \nیَا مَنْ جَادَ بِلُطْفِهٖ یَا مَنْ تَعَزَّزَ بِقُدْرَتِهٖ\nYAA MAN JAADA BE-LUTFEHI, YAA MAN TA-A’ZZAZA BE-QUDRATEHI, \nO He Who is effectually kind, O He Who confers honour with authority, \nیَا مَنْ قَدَّرَ بِحِكْمَتِهٖ یَا مَنْ حَكَمَ بِتَدْبِیْرِهٖ\nYAA MAN QADDARA BE-HIMMATEHI, YAA MAN HAKAMA BE-TADBEEREHI,\nO He Who ordains with wisdom, O He Who arbitrates with discretion, \nیَا مَنْ دَبَّرَ بِعِلْمِهٖ یَا مَنْ تَجَاوَزَ بِحِلْمِهٖ\nYAA MAN DABBARA BE-I’LMEHI, YAA MAN TAJAWAZA BE-HILMEHI,\nO He Who directs through knowledge, O He Who is indulgent out of forbearance, \nیَا مَنْ دَنٰی فِیْ عُلُوِّهٖ یَا مَنْ عَلاَ فِیْ دُنُوِّهٖ.\nYAA MAN DANA FEE O’LUWWEHI, YAA MAN A’LAA FEE ZONUWWEHI.\nO He Who is near in spite of highness, O He Who is High notwithstanding the nearness.\n(83) To Cure Backache\nیَا مَنْ یَّخْلُقُ مَا یَشَآءُ یَا مَنْ یَفْعَلُ مَا یَشَآءُ\nYAA MANY YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAA-O’, YAA MANY YAF-A’LO MAA YASHAA-O’, \nO He Who creates whatever He wants, O He Who does Whatever He wills, \nیَا مَنْ یَهْدِیْ مَنْ یَّشَآءُ یَا مَنْ یُّضِلُّ مَنْ یَّشَآءُ\nYAA MANY YAHDI MAN YASHAA-O’, YAA MANY YOZILLO MAYN YASHAA-O’, \nO He Who guides whomsoever He chooses, O He Who abandons whomsoever he desieres, \nیَا مَنْ یُّعَذِّبُ مَنْ یَّشَآءُ یَا مَنْ یَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ یَّشَآءُ\nYAA MANY YO-A’ZZEBO MAYN YASHAA-O’, YAA MANY YAGHFERO LEMAYN-YASHAA-O’, \nO He Who punishes Whomsoever He condemns, O He Who forgives whomsoever He prefers, \nیَا مَنْ یُعِزُّ مَنْ یَّشَآءُ یَا مَنْ یُضِلُّ مَنْ یَّشَآءُ\nYAA MANY YO-I’ZZO MAYN YASHAA-O’, YAA MANY YOZILLO MAYN YASHAA-O \nO He Who elevates whom-soever He takes up, O He Who humiliates whomsoever He dislikes, \nیَا مَنْ یُّصَوِّرُ فِی الْاَرْحَامِ مَا یَشَآءُ یَا مَنْ یَّخْتَصُّ بِرَحْمَتِهٖ مَنْ یَّشَآءُ.\nYAA MANY YOSAWWERO FIL-ARHAAME MAA YASHAA-O’, YAA MANY YAKHTASSO BE-RAHMATEHI MAYN-YASHAA-O’.\nO He Who gives shape (to bodies) in the wombs howsoever He likes, O He Who elects, with His mercy, whomsoever He favours.\n(84) To Cure Pain In The Right Ribs\nیَا مَنْ لَّمْ یَتَّخِذْ صَاحِبَۃً وَّلاَ وَلَدًا\nYAA MAN LAM YATTAKHIZ SAAHEBATAN WA LAA WALADAN, \nO He Who did not take to wife, nor beget children, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ لِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدْرًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LA LE KULLE SHAY-IN QADRA, \nO He Who took stock of the utility of all things, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُشْرِكُ فِی حُكْمِهٖ اَحَدًا\nYAA MAN-LAA YUSHREKO FEE HUKMEHI AHADAN, \nO He Who does not share with anyone to issue His orders, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ الْمَلَآئِكَۃَ رُسُلًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAL MALAA-EKATA ROSOLAN, \nO He Who selected Angels as messengers, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ فِی السَّمَآءِ بُرُوْجًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LA FIS-SAMAA-E BOROOJAN \nO He Who appointed stations in the heavens, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ الْاَرْضَ قَرَارًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LAL ARZA QARAARAN, \nO He Who rendered the earth stable and steady, \nیَا مَنْ خَلَقَ مِنَ الْمَآءِ بَشَرًا\nYAA MAN KHALAQA MENAL MAAA-E BASHARAN, \nO He Who creates man from the sperm, \nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَ لِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ اَمَدًا\nYAA MAN JA-A’LA LE-KULLE SHAY-IN AMADAN, \nO He Who determines limits for all things, \nیَا مَنْ اَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ عِلْمًا\nYAA MAN AHAATA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN I’LMAN, \nO He Who is aware of everything thorough knowledge, \nیَا مَنْ اَحْصٰی كُلَّ شَیْءٍ عَدَدًا.\nYAA MAN AHSA KULLA SHAY-IN A’DADAN.\nO He Who enumerates the calculation (terms) of everything.\n(85) To Cure Pain In The Waist\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا اَوَّلُ یَا اٰخِرُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA AWWALO, YAA AAKHERO,\nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O First, O Last, \nیَا ظَاهِرُ یَا بَاطِنُ یَا بَرُّ یَا حَقُّ\nYAA ZAAHERO, YAA BAATENO, YAA BARRO, YAA HAQQO, \nO Hidden, O Evident, O Pious, O Real, \nیَا فَرْدُ یَا وِتْرُ یَا صَمَدُ یَا سَرْمَدُ.\nYAA FARDO, YAA WITRO, YAA SAMADO, YAA SARMADO.\nO Single, O One and Only, O Independent, O Ever-Lasting.\n(86) To Cure Spleen Ailments\nیَا خَیْرَ مَعْرُوْفٍ عُرِفَ یَا اَفْضَلَ مَعْبُوْدٍ عُبِدَ\nYAA KHAYRA MA’ROOFIN O’OREFA YAA AFZALA MA’BOODIN O’BEDA, \nO Well-Known, thoroughly acknowledged, O Most Excellent Worship able, devotedly worshiped, \nیَا اَجَلَّ مَشْكُوْرٍ شُكِرَ یَا اَعَزَّ مَذْكُوْرٍ ذُكِرَ\nYAA AJALLA MASHKOORIN SHOKERA, YAA A-A’ZZA MAZKOORIN ZOKERA, \nO Most Illustrious Thank-Worthy, gratefully thanked, O Dearest Memorable, sincerely remembered, \nیَا اَعْلٰی مَحْمُوْدٍ حُمِدَ یَا اَقْدَمَ مَوْجَوْدٍ طُلِبَ\nYAA A-A’LAA MAHMOODIN HOMEDA, YAA AQDAMA MAWJOODIN TOLEBA, \nO Highest Praiseworthy, thankfully praised, O Foremost Supreme Being, longingly beseeched, \nیَا اَرْفَعَ مَوْصُوْفٍ وُصِفَ یَا اَكْبَرَ مَقْصُوْدٍ قُصِدَ\nYAA ARFA-A’ MAWSOOFIN WOSEFA, YAA AKBARA MAQSOODIN QOSEDA, \nO Most Elated Attributable, distinguishedly described, O The Greatest purpose, eagerly strived for, \nیَا اَكْرَمَ مَسْئُوْلٍ سُئِلَ یَا اَشْرَفَ مَحْبُوْبٍ عُلِمَ.\nYAA AKRAMA MAS-O’OLIN SO-ELA, YAA ASHRAFA MAHBOOBIN O’LEMA.\nO Most Generous entreatingly requested, O Noblest Beloved, ardently recognised.\n(87) To Cure Headache\nیَا حَبِیْبَ الْبَاكِیْنَ یَا سَیِّدَ الْمُتَوَكِّلِیْنَ \nYAA HABEEBAL BAAKEENA YAA SAYYEDAL MOTAWAKKELEENA, \nO Friend of the grief stricken, O Firm Supporter of those who rely upon (Him), \nیَا هَادِیَ الْمُضِلِّیْنَ یَا وَلِیَّ الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ \nYAA HAADEYAL MOZILLEENA, YAA WALIYYAL MO-AMENEENA, \nO Guide of the wayward, O Guardian of the faithful, \nیَا اَنِیْسَ الذَّاكِرِیْنَ یَا مَفْزَعَ الْمَلْهُوْفِیْنَ \nYAA ANEESAZ ZAAKEREENA, YAA MAFZA-A’L MALHOOFEENA, \nO Companion of the rememberers, O Refuge of the unhappy, \nیَا مُنْجِیَ الصَّادِقِیْنَ یَا اَقْدَرَ الْقَادِرِیْنَ \nYAA MUNJEYAS SAADEQEENA, YAA AQDARAL QAADREENA, \nO Redeemer of the truthful, O the Most Powerful of powerfuls, \nیَا اَعْلَمَ الْعَالِمِیْنَ یَا اِلٰهَ الْخَلْقِ اَجْمَعِیْنَ.\nYAA A-A’LAMAL A’ALEMEENA YAA ELAAHAL KHALQE AJMAE’ENA.\nO The Best of knowers, O God of all creation.\n(88) To Cure Pain In Forehead\nیَا مَنْ عَلَا فَقَهَرَ یَا مَنْ مَّلَكَ فَقَدَرَ \nYAA MAN A’LAA FAQAHARA, YAA MAN MALAKA FAQADARA, \nO He Who is High so overpowers, O He Who is Master so preordains, \nیَا مَنْ بَطَنَ فَخَبَرَ یَا مَنْ عُبِدَ فَشَكَرَ \nYAA MAN BATANA FAKHABARA, YAA MAN O’BEDA FASHAKARA \nO He Who penetrates hearts so is aware, O He Who is worshiped and acknowledges, \nیَا مَنْ عُصِیَ فَغَفَرَ یَا مَنْ لَّا تَحْوِیْهِ الْفِكَرُ \nYAA MAN O’SEYA FAGHAFARA YAA MAN LAA TAHWEEHIL FEKARO, \nO He Who is disobeyed yet forgives, O He Whom intellect cannot grasp, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُدْرِكُهٗ بَصَرٌ یَا مَنْ لَّا یَخْفٰی عَلَیْهِ اَثَرٌ \nYAA MAN LA YOODREKOHU BASARUN YAA MAN LAA YAKHFAA A’LAYHE ASARUN \nO He Whom insight cannot conceive, O He from Whose investigation nothing can be kept secret, \nیَا رَازِقَ الْبَشَرِ یَا مُقَدِّرَ كُلِّ قَدَرٍ.\nYAA RAAZEQAL BASHARE, YAA MOQADDERA KULLE QADARIN.\nO Provider of livelihood, O Ordainer of every destiny.\n(89) To Cure Non-Stop Urination\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا حَافِظُ یَا بَارِءُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA HAAFEZO, YAA BAAREO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Guardian, O Creator, \nیَا ذَارِءُ یَا بَاذِخُ یَا فَارِجُ یَا فَاتِحُ\nYAA ZAAREO YAA BAAZEKHO, YAA FAAREJO, YAA FAATEHO, \nO Multiplier, O Very Proud, O Reliever, O Conqueror, \nیَا كَاشِفُ یَا ضَامِنُ یَا اٰمِرُ یَا نَاهِیْ.\nYAA KAASHEFO, YAA ZAAMENO YAA AAMERO, YAA NAHEYO.\nO Investigator, O Guarantor, O Governor, O Prohibiter.\n(90) To Cure Pain In Navel\nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَعْلَمُ الْغَیْبَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YA’LAMUL GHAYBA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, knows the unknown, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یَصْرِفُ السُّوْٓءَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YASREFUS SOO-A ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, drives away evil, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَخْلُقُ الْخَلْقَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YAKHLOQUL KHALQA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, creates the creation, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوْبَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YAGHFERUZ ZONOOBA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, forgives the sins, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُتِمُّ النِّعْمَۃَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YOTIMMUN NEA’-MATA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, effects the bounties, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُقَلِّبُ الْقُلُوْبَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YOQALLEBUL QOLOOBA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, makes hearts turn to (Him), \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YODABBERUL AMRA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, directs administration, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُنَزِّلُ الْغَیْثَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YONAZZELUL GHAYSA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and no one else, sends down abundant and far-spread rain, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nYAA MAN LAA YABSOTUR RIZQA ILLAA HOWA, \nO He Who alone, and on one else, liberally distributes sustenance, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُحْیِ الْمَوْتٰی اِلَّا هُوَ.\nYAA MAN LAA YOHYIL-MAWTA ILLAA HOWA.\nO He Who alone, and no one else, brings back the dead to life.\n(91) To Remove The Stone From Bladder\nیَا مُعِیْنَ الضُّعَفَآءِ یَا صَاحِبَ الْغُرَبَآءِ\nYAA MO-E’ENAZ ZOAFAA-E, YAA SAAHEBAL GHORA-BAA-E, \nO Supporter of the weak, O Companion of the forsaken, \nیَا نَاصِرَ الْاَوْلِیَآءِ یَا قَاهِرَ الْاَعْدَآءِ\nYAA NAASERAL AWLEYAA-E, YAA QAAHERAL A-A’DAA-E,\nO Helper of friends, O Subduer of enemies,\nیَا رَافِعَ السَّمَآءِ یَا اَنِیْسَ الْاَصْفِیَآءِ\nYAA RAAFEAS SAMAA-E YAA ANEESAL ASFEYAA-E, \nO Raiser of the sky, O Comrade of the sincerely attached, \nیَا حَبِیْبَ الْاَتْقِیَآءِ یَا كَنْزَ الْفُقَرَآءِ\nYAA HABEEBAL ATQEYAA-E, YAA KANZAL FOQARAA-E,\nO Friend of the pious, O En-richer of the have nots, \nیَآ اِلٰهَ الْاَغْنِیَآءِ یَا اَكْرَمَ الْكُرَمَآءِ.\nYAA ELAAHAL AGHNEYAA-E, YAA AKRAMAL KORAMAA-E.\nO God of the rich, O Honourer of the generous.\n(92) To Cure Piles\nیَا كَافِیَ مِنْ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ\nYAA KAAFEYA MIN KULLE SHAY-IN \nO Able to do all things, \nیَآ قَائِمًا عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ\nYAA QAA-E’MO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN, \nO Lasting beyond all things, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُشْبِهُهٗ شَیْءٌ\nYAA MAN LAA YUSHBEHOHU SHAY-UN, \nO He like unto Whom there is nothing, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَزِیْدُ فِی مُلْكِهٖ شَیْءٌ\nYAA MAN LAA YAZEEDO FEE MULKEHI SHAY-UN, \nO He in Whose kingdom nothings can be added, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَخْفٰی عَلَیْهِ شَیْءٌ\nYAA MAN LAA YAKHFA A’LAYHE SHAY-UN, \nO He from Whom nothing is hidden, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَنْقُصُ مِنْ خَزَآئِنِهٖ شَیْءٌ\nYAA MAN LAA YANQOSO FEE KHAZAA-E’NEHI SHAY-UN, \nO He Whose treasure never diminishes, \nیَا مَنْ لَیْسَ كَمِثْلِهٖ شَیْءٌ\nYAA MAN LAYSA KAMISLEHI SHAY-UN, \nO He Comparable unto Whom there is nothing, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَعْزُبُ عَنْ عِلْمِهٖ شَیْءٌ\nYAA MAN LAA YAGHRABO A’N I’LMEHI SHAY-UN, \nO He from Whose knowledge nothing is missing,\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ خَبِیْرٌ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ\nYAA MAN HOWA KHABEERUN BE-KULLE SHAY-UN, \nO He Who is aware of all things, \nیَا مَنْ وَسِعَتْ رَحْمَتُهٗ كُلَّ شَیْءٍ.\nYAA MAN WASE-A’T RAHMATOHU KULLA SHAY-IN.\nO He Whose mercy extends to everything.\n(93) To Cure Ulcers\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا مُكْرِمُ یَا مُطْعِمُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA MUKREMO, YAA MUT-E’MO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Who grants benefits, O Who gives food, \nیَا مُنْعِمُ یَا مُعْطِیْ یَا مُغْنِیْ یَا مُقْنِیْ \nYAA MUN-E’MO, YAA MOA’TEE, YAA MUGHNEE, YAA MUQNEE, \nO Who bestows bounties, O Who awards rewards, O Who makes rich, O Who gives happiness,\nيَا مُفْنِیْ یَا مُحْیِیْ یَا مُرْضِیْ یَا مُنْجِیْ.\nYAA MUFNEE, YAA MOHYEE, YAA MURZEE, YAA MUNJEE.\nO Who destroys, O Who brings back to life, O Who satisfies, O Who rescues.\n(94) To Cure Nose Ailments\nیَآ اَوَّلَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ اٰخِرَهٗ\nYAA AWWALA KULLE SHAY-IN WA A’AKHERAHU \nO Beginning and End of all things, \nیَا اِلٰهَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّمَلِیْكَهٗ\nYAA ELAAHA KULLE SHAY-IN WA MALEEKAHU, \nO God and King of all things, \nیَا رَبَّ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ صَانِعَهٗ\nYAA RABBA KULLE SHAY-IN WA SAANE-A’HU, \nO Lord and maker of all things, \nیَا بَارِءَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ خَالِقَهٗ\nYAA BAAREA KULLE SHAY-IN WA KHALEQAHU \nO Originator and Creator of all things, \nیَا قَابِضَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ بَاسِطَهٗ\nYAA QAABEZA KULLE SHAY-IN WA BAASETAHU,\nO Seizer and Spreader of all things,\nیَا مُبْدِءَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ مُعِیْدَهٗ\nYAA MUBDE-A’ KULLE SHAY-IN WA MO-E’EDAHU,\nO Inventor and Resurrecter of all things,\nیَا مُنْشِئَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ مُقَدِّرَهٗ\nYAA MUNSHE-A KULLE SHAY-IN WA MOQADDERAHU, \nO Author and Pre-ordainer of all things,\nیَا مُكَوِّنَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ مُحَوِّلَهٗ\nYAA MOKAWWENA KULLE SHAY-IN WA MOHAWWELAHU,\nO Establisher and Abolisher of all things,\nیَا مُحْیِیَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ مُمِیْتَهٗ\nYAA MOHYE-YA KULLE SHAY-IN WA MOMEETAHU,\nO Who brings everything to life and puts everything to death,\nیَا خَالِقَ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ وَّ وَارِثَهٗ.\nYAA KHAALEQA KULLE SHAY-IN WA WAARESAHU.\nO Producer and Possessioner of all things.\n(95) To Cure Stomachache\nیَا خَیْرَ ذَاكِرٍ وَّ مَذْكُوْرٍ\nYAA KHAYRA ZAAKERIN WA MAZKOORIN, \nO Who remembers excellently and likewise is remembered,\nیَّا خَیْرَ شَاكِرِوَّ مَشْكُوْرٍ\nYAA KHAYRA SHAKERIN WA MASHKOORIN, \nO Who expresses appreciation excellently and likewise is appreciated, \nیَا خَیْرَ حَامِدٍ وَّ مَحْمُوْدٍ\nYAA KHAYRA HAAMEDIN WA MAHMOODIN, \nO Who Priases excellently and likewise is praised, \nیَا خَیْرَ شَاهِدٍ وَّ مَشْهُوْدٍ\nYAA KHAYRA SHAAHEDIN WA MASH-HOODIN, \nO Who bears testimony excellently and likewise is testified, \nیَا خَیْرَ دَاعٍ وَّ مَدْعُوٍّ\nYAA KHAYRA DAA-I’N WA MAD-O’OWWIN, \nO Who calls up excellently and likewise is called upon, \nیَا خَیْرَ مُجِیْبٍ وَّ مُجَابٍ\nYAA KHAYRA MOJEEBIN WA MOOJAABIN, \nO Who gives response excellently and likewise is responded, \nیَا خَیْرَ مُوْنِسٍ وَّ اَنِیْسٍ\nYAA KHAYRA MOONESIN WA ANEESIN\nO Excellent sympathizer and consoler, \nیَا خَیْرَ صَاحِبٍ وَّ جَلِیْسٍ\nYAA KHAYRA SAAHEBIN WA JALEESIN, \nO Excellent Companion and comrade, \nیَا خَیْرَ مَقْصُوْدٍ وَّ مَطْلُوْبٍ\nYAA KHAYRA MAQSOODIN WA MATLOOBIN,\nO Excellent Goal and Aim, \nیَا خَیْرَ حَبِیْبٍ وَّ مَحْبُوْبٍ.\nYAA KHAYRA HABEEBIN WA MAHBOOBIN.\nO Excellent Intimate and Beloved.\n(96) To Cure Knee Pain\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ لِمَنْ دَعَاهُ مُجِیْبُ\nYAA MAN HOWA LEMAN DA-AA’HO MOJEEBUN,\nO He Who answers to him who calls out, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ لِمَنْ اَطَاعُهٗ حَبِیْبٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA LEMAN ATAA-A’HU HABEEBUN, \nO He Who is ally of him who obeys, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ اِلٰی مَنْ اَحَبَّهٗ قَرِیْبٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA ELAA MAN AHABBAHU QAREEBUN, \nO He Who is near to him who loves (Him), \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ بِمَنِ اسْتَحْفَظَهٗ رَقِیْبٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA BEMANIS TAHFAZAHU RAQEEBUN, \nO He Who is sentinel of him who asks for (His) protection, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ بِمَنْ رَجَاهُ كَرِیْمٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA BEMAN RAJAAHO KAREEMUN, \nO He Who is Generous to him who makes a request (to Him), \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ بِمَنْ عَصَاهٗ حَلِیْمٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA BEMAN A’SAAHO HALEEMUN\nO He Who is indulgent towards him who disobeys, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ عَظَمَتِهٖ رَحِیْمٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE A’ZAMATEHI RAHEEMOON,\nO He Who, in His greatness, is Merciful, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ حِكْمَتِهٖ عَظِیْمٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE HIKMATEHI A’ZEEMUN,\nO He Who, in His wisdom is great, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ فِیْ اِحْسَانِهٖ قَدِیْمٌ\nYAA MAN HOWA FEE EHSAANEHI QADEEMUN,\nO He Who, in His benevolence, is foremost, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ بِمَنْ اَرَادَهٗ عَلِیْمٌ.\nYAA MAN HOWA BEMAN ARAADAHU A’LEEMUN.\nO He Who is aware of him who desires (Him).\n(97) To Cure Throat Pain\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ یَا مُسَبِّبُ یَا مُرَغِّبُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BISMEKA YAA MOSABBEBO, YAA MORAGHGHEBO, \nO Allah I beseech You in Your name, O Prime Cause, O Who inspires desires, \nیَا مُقَلِّبُ یَا مُعَقِّبُ یَا مُرَتِّبُ یَا مُخَوِّفُ\nYAA MOQALLEBO, YAA MO-A’QQEBO, YAA MORATTEBO, YAA MOKHAWWEFO, \nO Who makes adjustments, O Who punishes, O Who arranges, O Who alarms, \nیَا مُحَذِّرُ یَا مُذَكِّرُ یَا مُسَخِّرُ یَا مُغَیِّرُ.\nYAA MOHAZZERO, YAA MOZAKKERO, YAA MOSAKHKHERO, YAA MOGHAYYERO.\nO Who warns, O Who reminds, O Who subdues, O Who transforms.\n(98) To Seek Fulfilment of Legitimate Desire\nیَا مَنْ عِلْمُهٗ سَابِقٌ یَا مَنْ وَعْدُهٗ صَادِقٌ\nYAA MAN I’LMOHU SAABEQUN, YAA MAN WA’DOHU SAADEQUN,\nO He Whose knowledge is a priori, O He Whose promise is true,\nیَا مَنْ لُطْفُهٗ ظَاهِرٌ یَا مَنْ اَمْرُهٗ غَالِبٌ\nYAA MAN LUTFOHU ZAAHERUN, YAA MAN AMROHU GHALEBUN, \nO He Whose kindness is evident, O He Whose command is prevalent, \nیَا مَنْ كِتَابُهٗ مُحْكَمٌ یَا مَنْ قَضَآءُهٗ كَآئِنٌ\nYAA MAN KETAABOHU MOHKAMUN, YAA MAN QAZAA-A’HU KAA-ENUN,\nO He Whose Book is certain, O He Whose decision is carried through, \nیَا مَنْ قُرْاٰنُهٗ مَجِیْدٌ یَا مَنْ مُلْكُهٗ قَدِیْمٌ\nYAA MAN QURAANOHU MAJEEDUN, YAA MAN MULKOHU QADEEMUN, \nO He Whose Quran is glorious, O He Whose kingdom is eternal, \nیَا مَنْ فَضْلُهٗ عَمِیْمٌ یَا مَنْ عَرْشُهٗ عَظِیْمٌ.\nYAA MAN FAZLOHU A’MEEMUN, YAA MAN ARSHOHU A’ZEEMUN.\nO He Whose favour is all-embracing, O He Whose throne is sublime.\n(99) To Cure Pain In Legs\nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَشْغَلُهٗ سَمْعٌ عَنْ سَمْعٍ\nYAA MAN LAA YASH-GHOLOHU SAM-U’N A’N SAM-I’N, \nO He Whom one audience does not keep away from hearing another, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَمْنَعُهٗ فِعْلٌ عَنْ فِعلٍ\nYAA MAN LAA YAMNA-O’HU FEA’LUN A’N FEA’LIN, \nO He Whom one action does not prevent from executing another, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُلْهِیْهِ قَوْلٌ عَنْ قَوْلٍ\nYAA MAN LAA YULHEEHE QAWLUN A’N QAWLIN,\nO He Whom one address does not prevent from delivering another, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُغَلِّطُهٗ سُؤَالٌ عَنْ سُؤَالٍ\nYAA MAN LAA YOGHALLETOHU SO-A’LUN A’N SO-A’LIN,\nO He Whom one question does not draw apart from another, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یَحْجُبُهٗ شَیْءٌ عَنْ شَیْءٍ\nYAA MAN LAA YAHJOBOHU SHAY-IN A’N SHAY-IN \nO He for Whom one object does not get in the way of another, \nیَا مَنْ لَّا یُبْرِمُهٗ اِلحَاحُ الْمُلِحِّیْنَ\nYAA MAN LAA YUBREMOHU ILHAAHUL MOLEHHEENA\nO He Whom importunity of intimidators does not make ill-tempered, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ غَایَۃُ مُرَادِ الْمُرِیْدِیْنَ\nYAA MAN HOWA GHAAYATO MORAADIL MOREEDEENA,\nO He Who is the Last resort of the wishes of the devotees, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ مُنْتَهٰی هِمَمِ الْعَارِفِیْنَ\nYAA MAN HOWA MUNTAHAA HEMAMIL A’AREFEENA,\nO He Who is the ultimate goal of the aspirations of the intelligent, \nیَا مَنْ هُوَ مُنْتَهٰی طَلَبِ الطَّالِبِیْنَ\nYAA MAN HOWA MUN-TAHAA TALABIT TAALEBEENA,\nO He Who is the ultimate means of fulfilment of the beseechers, \nیَا مَنْ لَا یَخْفٰی عَلَیْهِ ذَرَّۃٌ فِی الْعَالَمِیْنَ.\nYAA MAN LAA YAKHFA A’LAYHE ZARRATUN FIL A’ALAMEENA.\nO He from Whom not even the minutest unit matter is hidden.\n(100) To Cure Thigh Pain\nیَا حَلِیْمًا لَا یَعْجَلُ یَا جَوَادًا لَا یَبْخَلُ\nYAA HALEEMAN LAA YA’JALO, YAA JAWAADAN LAA YABKHALO, \nO Forbearing Who does not make haste, O Liberal Bestower Who never supplies sparingly, \nیَا صَادِقًا لَا یُخْلِفُ یَا وَهَّابًا لَا یَمَلُّ\nYAA SAADEQAN LAA YUKHLEFO, YAA WAHHAABAN LAA YAMALLO, \nO Truthful Who never turns away, O Awarder Who never regrets, \nیَاقَاهِرًا لَا یُغْلَبُ یَا عَظِیْمًا لَا یُوْصَفُ\nYAA QAAHERAN LAA YUGHLABO, YAA A’ZEEMAN LAA YOOSAFO, \nO Dominant Who is never overpowered, O Sublime Who cannot be described, \nیَا عَدْلًا لَا یَحِیْفُ یَا غَنِیًّا لَا یَفْتَقِرُ\nYAA A’DLAN LAA YAHEEFO, YAA GHANIYYAN LAA YAFTAQERO \nO Just Who does not oppress, O Rich Who cannot be rendered poor, \nیَا كَبِیْرًا لَا یَصْغُرُ یَا حَافِظًا لَّا یَغْفُلُ.\nYAA KABEERAN LAA YASGHORO YAA HAAFEZAN LAA YAGHFOLO.\nO Great Who cannot be rendered small, O Guardian Who does not neglect."
